{"drafts":[{"assumptions":["ASM-24 (Stripe card payments) conflicts with request section 32, which says the portal takes no online card payments in this phase. This spec follows the request: staff record payment manually with a payment date and the system records who did it.","An ERP file fails validation as a whole if it is empty, is missing a required column, or has any row whose quantity is not a non-negative integer. Unknown product identifiers alone do not fail the file (ASM-6).","Stock import rows are matched to products by distributor product code until the client supplies the column layout (ASM-7). Products missing from a valid file keep their previous quantity, and a product never imported counts as Out of stock.","Price validation at checkout rejects the submission and lists changed lines so the Buyer can review them again. It does not silently reprice the order.","Repeat order adds lines at their original quantity, capped at available stock and flagged when reduced.","Order totals are net (tax-exclusive). Tax and gross appear only on invoices (ASM-9).","A deactivated price list cannot be newly assigned to a company.","Search is a case-insensitive substring match. Ranking is not specified.","Vehicle compatibility entries store a model-year range (from–to).","Confirmation validation means: every line is within available stock and the delivery address still exists.","A password reset request returns the same response whether or not the email exists, so it can't be used to discover which emails have accounts.","The stock quantity limit (ASM-4) applies to staff-created order lines as well as Buyer baskets.","The sales report counts only Delivered orders, by delivery date, at net order-time prices.","Product images may be JPEG, PNG or WebP (ASM-29 sets the 10 MB limit).","Delivery list CSV columns are those in REQ-54 until the client confirms them.","The session idle timeout of 30 minutes (NFR-9) is our assumption. The request only says 'session management'."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"p95 response time ≤ 1.5 s with 50,000 active products and 100 concurrent signed-in users","text":"Catalogue search, category filter and vehicle search respond quickly under load."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"p95 response time ≤ 2 s at 100 concurrent users","text":"Other API calls (basket, order, invoice list) respond within a bounded time."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"A 100,000-row CSV is validated and applied in ≤ 15 minutes","text":"The nightly ERP stock import completes within its window."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"≥ 99% of emails handed off within 5 minutes of the event","text":"Order and account emails are handed to the email service promptly after the triggering event."},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"0 plaintext or reversibly encrypted passwords; argon2id or bcrypt with cost ≥ 12","text":"Passwords are stored only as salted adaptive hashes."},{"id":"NFR-6","metric":"100% of endpoints served over TLS 1.2 or higher; 0 plain-HTTP endpoints","text":"All traffic is encrypted in transit."},{"id":"NFR-7","metric":"0 records of another company returned in an automated isolation suite covering 100% of Buyer-accessible endpoints","text":"Cross-company data isolation for Buyers."},{"id":"NFR-8","metric":"0 outbound write calls to ERP systems or the ERP drop location","text":"The portal never writes to the ERP."},{"id":"NFR-9","metric":"Session token rejected after 30 minutes without a request","text":"Sessions expire after inactivity."},{"id":"NFR-10","metric":"≥ 99.5% monthly uptime excluding announced maintenance","text":"Availability of the portal."},{"id":"NFR-11","metric":"Fully usable in the latest 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari at viewport widths from 360 px to 1920 px","text":"Responsive web support."},{"id":"NFR-12","metric":"p95 ≤ 5 s for an invoice with up to 200 lines","text":"Invoice PDF generation time."}],"outOfScope":["Customer Account Manager role (Q-1)","Saved basket templates (ASM-1)","Buyers creating or editing their own delivery addresses (Q-7, ASM-13)","Basket persistence across sessions (ASM-14)","Nested categories (ASM-15)","Separate Rejected order status; rejection uses Cancelled with a reason (ASM-16)","SMS and push notifications (ASM-17, ASM-18)","Full field-level audit trail beyond created/last-changed by and at, status timeline and amendment records (ASM-21)","Custom report builder (ASM-20)","Migration of existing customer, product, price or vehicle data; system starts empty with seed data (ASM-22)","CSV upload of vehicle compatibility data (ASM-23)","Native mobile apps (ASM-30)","Languages other than English (ASM-10)","Backorders (request section 8)","Online card payments and partial payments (request section 32)","Route planning (request section 22)","Volume, promotional and date-effective pricing and discounts (request section 10: one price per product per price list)","Any modification of ERP stock (request section 9)"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active Buyer account buyer@a.test with a known password","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response contains a session token and the role value \"Buyer\"","when":"POST to the sign-in endpoint with that email and password"},{"given":"The session token returned in AC-1.1","id":"AC-1.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned email field is buyer@a.test","when":"The user requests their own account details with that token"}],"ears":"When a user submits an email address and password that match an active account, the portal shall start an authenticated session and return the user's role.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active account buyer@a.test","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401 and the error message is \"Invalid email or password\"","when":"POST to the sign-in endpoint with a wrong password"},{"given":"No account exists for ghost@x.test","id":"AC-2.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401 and the error message is identical to the one in AC-2.1","when":"POST to the sign-in endpoint with ghost@x.test and any password"}],"ears":"If a sign-in attempt uses an unknown email address or a wrong password, then the portal shall reject it with one identical invalid-credentials error message.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active account that has just had 4 consecutive failed sign-in attempts","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"The correct-password response status is 423 and the error message says the account is temporarily locked","when":"A 5th attempt with a wrong password is made, followed 1 minute later by an attempt with the correct password"},{"given":"An account locked at time T","id":"AC-3.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and a session token is returned","when":"The correct password is submitted at T + 15 minutes + 1 second (test clock)"},{"given":"An account with 4 failed attempts followed by 1 successful sign-in","id":"AC-3.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 because the failure count reset after the success","when":"4 more failed attempts are made and then the correct password is submitted"}],"ears":"If an account has 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts, then the portal shall lock the account against sign-in for 15 minutes.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-37"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user deactivated by an administrator","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and the error message says the account is inactive","when":"The user signs in with the correct password"},{"given":"A Buyer whose customer company has been set inactive","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and the error message says the account is inactive","when":"The Buyer signs in with the correct password"},{"given":"A Buyer holding a valid session token","id":"AC-4.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401","when":"An administrator deactivates the Buyer and the Buyer then requests the order list with the same token"}],"ears":"If a deactivated user, or a user whose customer company is inactive, attempts to sign in or uses an existing session, then the portal shall reject the request.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user with a valid session token","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"The sign-out response status is 200 and the catalogue response status is 401","when":"The user calls the sign-out endpoint and then requests the catalogue with the same token"}],"ears":"When a signed-in user signs out, the portal shall invalidate that user's session token.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"No session token","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"Each response status is 401 and no product, order or invoice data is returned","when":"GET the catalogue, an order and an invoice PDF"}],"ears":"If a request to any endpoint other than sign-in, password reset and invitation acceptance carries no valid session token, then the portal shall reject it with status 401.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Buyer","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403","when":"The Buyer requests the staff order queue"},{"given":"A signed-in Office Staff user","id":"AC-7.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and no price list record is created","when":"The user POSTs a new price list"},{"given":"A signed-in Administrator","id":"AC-7.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200","when":"The Administrator requests the staff order queue"}],"ears":"If a user calls an endpoint outside the capabilities of their role (Buyer, Office Staff or Administrator, where Administrator includes all Office Staff capabilities), then the portal shall reject the request with status 403.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-6","I-17","Q-1","ASM-28"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer A of company A and order ORD-000200 of company B","id":"AC-8.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 404 and no order data is returned","when":"Buyer A requests ORD-000200"},{"given":"Company B has invoice INV-000050","id":"AC-8.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 404 and no file is returned","when":"Buyer A requests the PDF of INV-000050"},{"given":"Company B has a delivery address and a price list different from company A","id":"AC-8.3","level":"api","then":"The returned address list contains only company A addresses and the returned price value comes from company A's price list","when":"Buyer A lists delivery addresses and opens a product"}],"ears":"While a Buyer is signed in, the portal shall return only orders, invoices, prices, delivery addresses and account data that belong to the Buyer's own customer company.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-5","I-9","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An account exists for buyer@a.test","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 202 and exactly one email containing a reset link is sent to buyer@a.test","when":"POST a password reset request for buyer@a.test"},{"given":"No account exists for ghost@x.test","id":"AC-9.2","level":"api","then":"The response status and body equal those of AC-9.1 and no email is sent","when":"POST a password reset request for ghost@x.test"}],"ears":"When a password reset is requested for an email address, the portal shall send a reset email with a single-use link valid for the configured period (default 1 hour) if that email belongs to an account, and return the same response either way.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-18","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A reset link issued 10 minutes ago","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"The new-password sign-in response status is 200 and the old-password response status is 401","when":"The user submits a new password through it and then signs in with the new and the old password"},{"given":"A reset link that has already been used","id":"AC-10.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 and the error message says the link is invalid or expired","when":"A new password is submitted through it again"},{"given":"A reset link issued 61 minutes ago with the default validity","id":"AC-10.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 and the error message says the link is invalid or expired","when":"A new password is submitted through it"},{"given":"An account locked after 5 failed attempts","id":"AC-10.4","level":"api","then":"The sign-in response status is 200","when":"The user completes a password reset and signs in with the new password within the 15-minute lock period"}],"ears":"When a user submits a new password through an unexpired, unused reset link, the portal shall replace the password, invalidate the link and clear any sign-in lock on the account.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Administrator and active company A","id":"AC-11.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201, the user record has status \"pending\" and one invitation email is sent to new.buyer@a.test","when":"POST an invitation for new.buyer@a.test as Buyer of company A"},{"given":"A signed-in Administrator","id":"AC-11.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 and no user record is created","when":"POST an invitation with role \"Customer Account Manager\""},{"given":"A signed-in Administrator","id":"AC-11.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 and the error names the company field","when":"POST an invitation for a Buyer without a customer company"}],"ears":"When an administrator invites a user with name, email, a role of Buyer, Office Staff or Administrator and, for a Buyer, a customer company, the portal shall create a pending account and send an invitation email with a link valid for the configured period (default 7 days).","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","Q-1","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An invitation sent 2 days ago","id":"AC-12.1","level":"api","then":"The user record status is \"active\" and the sign-in response status is 200","when":"The invitee sets a password through the link and signs in"},{"given":"An invitation sent 8 days ago with the default validity","id":"AC-12.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 and the user record status stays \"pending\"","when":"The invitee tries to set a password through the link"}],"ears":"When an invited user sets a password through an unexpired invitation link, the portal shall activate the account.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A pending account with an unused invitation link L1","id":"AC-13.1","level":"api","then":"A new invitation email is sent and the response to using L1 has status 400","when":"The administrator resends the invitation and the invitee then uses L1"}],"ears":"When an administrator resends the invitation of a pending account, the portal shall invalidate the previous invitation link and send a new invitation email.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer B has placed 3 orders","id":"AC-14.1","level":"api","then":"B's user record status is \"deactivated\" and the returned list still contains B's 3 orders","when":"An administrator deactivates B and a staff user lists orders filtered by B's company"},{"given":"A deactivated user","id":"AC-14.2","level":"api","then":"The sign-in response status is 200","when":"An administrator reactivates the user and the user signs in"},{"given":"A Buyer user","id":"AC-14.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200","when":"An administrator changes the role to Office Staff and the user requests the staff order queue"},{"given":"Users of several roles and statuses","id":"AC-14.4","level":"api","then":"Each returned row contains the role, company and status fields","when":"An administrator lists users"}],"ears":"The portal shall let administrators list users with role, customer company and account status, change a user's role, associate a Buyer with a customer company, deactivate a user and reactivate a deactivated user, without deleting any of the user's orders or invoices.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active products \"Brake Pad Set\" (code BP-100, part number 0986494, brand Bosch) and \"Oil Filter\" (code OF-20, brand Mann)","id":"AC-15.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains Brake Pad Set and does not contain Oil Filter","when":"A Buyer searches \"brak\""},{"given":"The products of AC-15.1","id":"AC-15.2","level":"api","then":"Each returned list contains Brake Pad Set","when":"A Buyer searches \"86494\", then \"bp-1\", then \"bosch\""},{"given":"A retired product \"Brake Drum\"","id":"AC-15.3","level":"api","then":"The returned list does not contain Brake Drum","when":"A Buyer searches \"brake\""}],"ears":"When a Buyer searches the catalogue with a text term, the portal shall return active products whose name, distributor product code, manufacturer part number or brand contains the term, ignoring letter case.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active products in categories Filters and Brake system","id":"AC-16.1","level":"api","then":"Every returned product has the category value Filters","when":"A Buyer lists the catalogue filtered by Filters"},{"given":"The same products","id":"AC-16.2","level":"api","then":"The returned count equals the number of active products","when":"A Buyer lists the catalogue with no category filter"},{"given":"Active products \"Oil Filter\" (Filters) and \"Oil Pump\" (Engine parts)","id":"AC-16.3","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains Oil Filter only","when":"A Buyer searches \"oil\" filtered by Filters"}],"ears":"When a Buyer filters the catalogue by a category, the portal shall return only active products assigned to that category, combined with any search term.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P has a compatibility entry Ford, Focus, years 2015–2018, 1.0 EcoBoost, petrol","id":"AC-17.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains P","when":"A Buyer searches make Ford, model Focus, year 2017"},{"given":"The same product P","id":"AC-17.2","level":"api","then":"The returned list does not contain P","when":"A Buyer searches make Ford, model Focus, year 2010"},{"given":"The same product P","id":"AC-17.3","level":"api","then":"The returned list does not contain P","when":"A Buyer searches make Ford, model Focus, fuel type diesel"}],"ears":"When a Buyer searches by vehicle using any combination of make, model, year, engine, fuel type and variant, the portal shall return only active products with a compatibility entry that matches every supplied value.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active product with all fields populated and a price on the Buyer's price list","id":"AC-18.1","level":"api","then":"The returned row for that product contains imageUrl, name, productCode, manufacturer, unit, packSize, price and stockStatus fields with the stored values","when":"A Buyer lists the catalogue"}],"ears":"The portal shall return, for each product in a catalogue result list, its image URL, name, distributor product code, manufacturer, unit, pack size, the Buyer's price and stock status.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active product with 2 compatibility entries","id":"AC-19.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned compatibility list has 2 entries alongside the other listed fields","when":"A Buyer opens the product"},{"given":"An active product with imported quantity 0","id":"AC-19.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the stockStatus value is \"Out of stock\"","when":"A Buyer opens the product"},{"given":"A retired product","id":"AC-19.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 404","when":"A Buyer opens the product"}],"ears":"When a Buyer opens an active product, the portal shall return its image, name, product code, manufacturer, description, unit, pack size, the Buyer's price, stock status and compatible vehicles.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product X costs 50.00 on Standard and 40.00 on Workshop A, and company A is assigned Workshop A","id":"AC-20.1","level":"api","then":"The returned price value is 40.00","when":"A Buyer of company A opens product X"},{"given":"The setup of AC-20.1","id":"AC-20.2","level":"api","then":"The returned price value is 50.00","when":"An administrator assigns Standard to company A and the Buyer opens product X again"}],"ears":"The portal shall price every product shown to a Buyer from the price list assigned to the Buyer's customer company.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active product Y with no price on company A's price list","id":"AC-21.1","level":"api","then":"The returned price field is null and the priceLabel value is \"Price on request\"","when":"A Buyer of company A opens product Y"},{"given":"The same product Y","id":"AC-21.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422, the error says the product is price on request and the basket line count is unchanged","when":"The Buyer adds product Y to the basket"}],"ears":"If a product has no price on the Buyer's assigned price list, then the portal shall show the product as \"Price on request\" and reject adding it to the basket.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-11","ASM-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Administrator","id":"AC-22.1","level":"api","then":"The Fleet price list has 1 row for product X with value 32.00","when":"The administrator creates price list \"Fleet\", sets product X to 30.00 and then sets product X to 32.00"},{"given":"Price list Fleet containing product X","id":"AC-22.2","level":"api","then":"The price list row count for product X is 0","when":"The administrator removes product X from Fleet"},{"given":"A deactivated price list","id":"AC-22.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 and the company's assigned price list value is unchanged","when":"The administrator assigns it to a customer company"}],"ears":"The portal shall let administrators create, rename and deactivate price lists, set, edit and remove one price per product on a price list, and assign an active price list to a customer company.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Order ORD-000101 has a line for product X at unit price 40.00","id":"AC-23.1","level":"api","then":"The returned unit price value on the order line is 40.00","when":"The administrator changes product X to 45.00 on that price list and the order is opened"}],"ears":"When a price on a price list is changed or the list is reassigned, the portal shall leave the unit prices stored on existing orders and invoices unchanged.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Low-stock threshold 5","id":"AC-24.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned values are Out of stock, Low stock, Low stock and In stock","when":"The stock-status calculator's public method is called with quantities 0, 1, 5 and 6"},{"given":"Low-stock threshold 5","id":"AC-24.2","level":"unit","then":"The returned value is Out of stock","when":"The stock-status calculator is called for a product with no imported quantity"}],"ears":"The portal shall derive each product's stock status as Out of stock when its imported quantity is 0 or it has never been imported, Low stock when the quantity is at or below the configured low-stock threshold, and In stock when the quantity is above that threshold.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-12","ASM-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Products BP-100 (quantity 3) and OF-20 (quantity 0) and a valid CSV listing BP-100=12 and OF-20=4","id":"AC-25.1","level":"job","then":"The stored quantity values are BP-100=12 and OF-20=4, their stockStatus fields are recalculated, and an import log row has status \"success\" and rows-applied count 2","when":"The stock import job runs"},{"given":"No new file in the configured location since the last run","id":"AC-25.2","level":"job","then":"No stock quantity value changes","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"When the scheduled stock import finds a new ERP CSV file in the configured location that passes file validation, the portal shall replace the stored quantity of each listed known product and record a successful import log entry.","id":"REQ-25","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A valid CSV with BP-100=12 and ZZ-999=5, where ZZ-999 is not a known product","id":"AC-26.1","level":"job","then":"BP-100's stored quantity value is 12 and the import log row has status \"success\" with ZZ-999 in its skipped-identifiers list","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"If a valid ERP CSV contains rows with unknown product identifiers, then the portal shall skip those rows, apply the other rows and list the unknown identifiers in the import log entry.","id":"REQ-26","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","ASM-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Stored quantity BP-100=12 and a CSV missing the quantity column","id":"AC-27.1","level":"job","then":"BP-100's stored quantity value is still 12 and an import log row has status \"failed\" and a reason naming the missing column","when":"The stock import job runs"},{"given":"Stored quantity BP-100=12 and a CSV where one row has quantity \"abc\" and another has BP-100=20","id":"AC-27.2","level":"job","then":"BP-100's stored quantity value is still 12 and the import log row has status \"failed\"","when":"The stock import job runs"},{"given":"An empty CSV file","id":"AC-27.3","level":"job","then":"No stored quantity value changes and the import log row has status \"failed\"","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"If an ERP CSV fails file validation, then the portal shall keep every previous stock quantity unchanged and record a failed import log entry with the failure reason.","id":"REQ-27","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"One successful and one failed import","id":"AC-28.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned list has 2 rows with time, status, rowsApplied, skippedIdentifiers and failureReason fields","when":"A staff user lists stock imports"},{"given":"A signed-in Buyer","id":"AC-28.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403","when":"The Buyer lists stock imports"}],"ears":"When a staff user or administrator lists stock imports, the portal shall return each import's time, status, rows-applied count, skipped identifiers and failure reason.","id":"REQ-28","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product BP-100 with imported quantity 10","id":"AC-29.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 and the error message states 10 available","when":"A Buyer sets the basket quantity to 11"},{"given":"The same product","id":"AC-29.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned line quantity is 10","when":"A Buyer sets the basket quantity to 10"},{"given":"Product OF-20 with imported quantity 0","id":"AC-29.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 and the error message says the product is out of stock","when":"A staff user adds 1 of OF-20 to an order being created for company A"}],"ears":"If a basket line or a staff-created order line is set to a quantity greater than the product's imported stock quantity, then the portal shall reject the change with an error stating the available quantity.","id":"REQ-29","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-12","I-13","ASM-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product X at 12.50 and product Z at 4.00 on the Buyer's price list, both in stock","id":"AC-30.1","level":"api","then":"The returned line totals are 25.00 and 12.00 and the subtotal value is 37.00","when":"The Buyer adds 2 of X and 3 of Z"},{"given":"The basket from AC-30.1","id":"AC-30.2","level":"api","then":"The returned line count is 1 and the subtotal value is 25.00","when":"The Buyer removes the Z line"},{"given":"The basket from AC-30.1","id":"AC-30.3","level":"api","then":"The returned basket line count is 0","when":"The Buyer signs out, signs in again and requests the basket"},{"given":"An empty basket","id":"AC-30.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 and the error names the quantity field","when":"The Buyer adds product X with quantity 0"}],"ears":"The portal shall let a signed-in Buyer add products to, change line quantities in and remove lines from a basket kept for the current session, returning each line's unit price and line total and the basket subtotal.","id":"REQ-30","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Cutoff 14:00, Saturday and Sunday non-working, Monday 6 Oct 2026 a working day","id":"AC-31.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned values are Tuesday 7 Oct, Wednesday 8 Oct and Wednesday 8 Oct","when":"The delivery-date calculator's public earliestDeliveryDate method is called with Monday 13:00, Monday 14:00 and Monday 15:00"},{"given":"Cutoff 14:00, weekends non-working","id":"AC-31.2","level":"unit","then":"The returned values are the following Monday and the following Tuesday","when":"earliestDeliveryDate is called with Friday 13:00 and Friday 15:00"},{"given":"Cutoff 14:00 and Tuesday 7 Oct 2026 listed as a non-working date","id":"AC-31.3","level":"unit","then":"The returned value is Wednesday 8 Oct","when":"earliestDeliveryDate is called with Monday 6 Oct 13:00"},{"given":"Timezone Europe/London and cutoff 14:00","id":"AC-31.4","level":"unit","then":"The returned value is Tuesday","when":"earliestDeliveryDate is called with Monday 12:30 UTC during British Summer Time (13:30 local)"}],"ears":"The portal shall calculate the earliest delivery date, in the configured timezone, as the next working day when the order time is before the configured cutoff (default 14:00) and as the working day after the next working day when the order time is at or after the cutoff.","id":"REQ-31","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-11","ASM-36"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Maximum 14 days ahead, weekends non-working, current time Monday 10:00","id":"AC-32.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list starts with Tuesday, contains no Saturday or Sunday, and its last value is no later than 14 days after today","when":"A Buyer requests the selectable delivery dates"}],"ears":"When a user requests delivery dates for checkout or a staff order, the portal shall return only working days from the earliest delivery date up to the configured maximum number of days ahead.","id":"REQ-32","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Buyer basket with delivery date Tuesday chosen at Monday 13:50","id":"AC-33.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422, the error names the deliveryDate field and no order record is created","when":"The Buyer submits the order at Monday 14:05"},{"given":"A Buyer of company A","id":"AC-33.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 and the error names the deliveryAddress field","when":"The Buyer submits an order using a delivery address id of company B"}],"ears":"If a submitted order has a delivery date that is not selectable at submission time or a delivery address that does not belong to the customer company, then the portal shall reject the submission with an error naming the invalid field.","id":"REQ-33","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","Q-7","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A basket with 5 of BP-100 when 12 were in stock, and a stock import then sets BP-100 to 3","id":"AC-34.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409, the returned list of affected lines contains BP-100 with available quantity 3, and no order record is created","when":"The Buyer submits the order"},{"given":"A basket line for product X at 40.00, and the administrator then changes X to 42.00","id":"AC-34.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 and the returned affected line shows current price 42.00","when":"The Buyer submits the order"}],"ears":"If, at submission, any basket line exceeds available stock or has a current price different from the price returned in the basket, then the portal shall reject the submission and list the affected lines with their current price and available quantity.","id":"REQ-34","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Prefix ORD- and last order number ORD-000123","id":"AC-35.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the returned order has number ORD-000124, status Received, 2 lines with the basket unit prices, the note value and 1 timeline entry naming the Buyer","when":"A Buyer submits a valid basket with 2 lines and note \"Leave at rear gate\""},{"given":"The order from AC-35.1","id":"AC-35.2","level":"api","then":"The queue list contains ORD-000124 and the returned basket line count is 0","when":"A staff user lists the order queue and the Buyer requests the basket"}],"ears":"When a valid order is submitted, the portal shall create an order with the next sequential prefixed order number, its lines at order-time unit prices, a copy of the delivery address, the delivery date, the optional note, status Received and a first timeline entry, and then empty the basket.","id":"REQ-35","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-4","I-13","ASM-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Buyer with a 2-line basket, a selected address, date and note","id":"AC-36.1","level":"manual","then":"A person checks that the review page is shown with every listed item matching the basket and that the order is only created after pressing submit","when":"The Buyer proceeds to checkout in a browser"}],"ears":"When a Buyer proceeds to checkout, the portal shall display a final review page with the lines, quantities, unit prices, line totals, subtotal, delivery address, delivery date and note before the submit action.","id":"REQ-36","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","I-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A set inactive","id":"AC-37.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422, the error says the company is inactive and no order record is created","when":"A staff user submits a new order for company A"},{"given":"A Buyer whose session is still valid in the same request in which the administrator deactivates them (race checked at submission)","id":"AC-37.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401 or 403 and no order record is created","when":"The order submission is processed after deactivation"}],"ears":"If a user of an inactive customer company or a deactivated user submits an order, or staff try to create an order for an inactive customer company, then the portal shall reject it with an error.","id":"REQ-37","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","I-9","Q-5","Q-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An order placed by buyer@a.test","id":"AC-38.1","level":"api","then":"The confirmation email is sent to buyer@a.test only","when":"Staff confirm the order"},{"given":"An order created by staff for company A whose contact email is orders@a.test","id":"AC-38.2","level":"api","then":"The confirmation email is sent to orders@a.test only","when":"Staff confirm the order"}],"ears":"The portal shall send each order email to the Buyer who placed the order, or to the customer company's contact email when staff created the order.","id":"REQ-38","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-4","ASM-17","ASM-33"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A has 1 order by Buyer A1, 1 by Buyer A2 and 1 created by staff","id":"AC-39.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list has 3 rows, each with orderNumber, orderDate, deliveryDate, deliveryAddress, total and status fields","when":"Buyer A1 lists orders"}],"ears":"When a Buyer lists orders, the portal shall return every order of the Buyer's customer company, including orders placed by colleagues and by staff, with order number, order date, delivery date, delivery address, total and status.","id":"REQ-39","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-15","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An order that was amended by staff and then confirmed","id":"AC-40.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, the returned timeline has entries for Received and Confirmed with time and actor, and the amendments list contains the quantity change","when":"A Buyer of that company opens the order"},{"given":"An order containing a product that was later retired","id":"AC-40.2","level":"api","then":"The returned line still shows the product name, code and order-time unit price","when":"A Buyer opens the order"}],"ears":"When a Buyer of the order's company or a staff user opens an order, the portal shall return its number, order date, customer, delivery address, requested delivery date, current status, status timeline, lines with quantities, unit prices and line totals, order total, note and staff amendments.","id":"REQ-40","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-14","I-15","I-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order of company A placed by Buyer A2","id":"AC-41.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, the order status value is Cancelled and the last timeline entry names Buyer A1","when":"Buyer A1 cancels it"},{"given":"A Received order created by staff for company A","id":"AC-41.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the order status value is Cancelled","when":"Buyer A1 cancels it"}],"ears":"When a Buyer cancels an order of their own company that is in Received status, the portal shall set its status to Cancelled and add a timeline entry with the Buyer and time.","id":"REQ-41","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Confirmed order of the Buyer's company","id":"AC-42.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409, the error message tells the Buyer to contact the distributor office and the status value stays Confirmed","when":"The Buyer cancels it"}],"ears":"If a Buyer tries to cancel an order that is not in Received status, then the portal shall reject the request with an error telling the Buyer to contact the distributor office.","id":"REQ-42","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An old order with 4 of X (now 42.00, 10 in stock), 2 of R (now retired) and 6 of Z (now 3 in stock)","id":"AC-43.1","level":"api","then":"The returned basket has X with quantity 4 at 42.00, Z with quantity 3 flagged as reduced, and R listed as unavailable and not added","when":"The Buyer repeats the order"},{"given":"The same old order","id":"AC-43.2","level":"api","then":"The company's order count is unchanged","when":"The Buyer repeats it"}],"ears":"When a Buyer repeats an order of their company, the portal shall add each still-orderable line to the session basket at the current price and the original quantity, capped at available stock, and flag lines that are retired, out of stock or without a price, without creating an order.","id":"REQ-43","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Orders for companies A and B in statuses Received and Picking","id":"AC-44.1","level":"api","then":"Every returned row has customer A and status Received","when":"A staff user lists orders filtered by company A and status Received"},{"given":"Orders dated 1, 5 and 9 October","id":"AC-44.2","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains only the 5 October order","when":"A staff user lists orders with order date range 4–6 October"}],"ears":"When a staff user lists orders, the portal shall return orders of all customers with order number, customer, order date, requested delivery date, total and status, filtered by any supplied customer, order date range and status.","id":"REQ-44","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-14","I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Companies \"Northside Motors\" (account C-1001) and \"Fleetline\" (C-2002)","id":"AC-45.1","level":"api","then":"The first returned list contains only Northside Motors and the second only Fleetline, each with addresses, priceList and status fields","when":"A staff user searches \"north\" and then \"C-2002\""}],"ears":"When a staff user searches customers by name or account number, the portal shall return matching customer companies with their details, delivery addresses, assigned price list and active status.","id":"REQ-45","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product X with quantity 7 and prices on Standard and Workshop A","id":"AC-46.1","level":"api","then":"The returned quantity value is 7 and the returned price list has 2 entries","when":"A staff user opens product X"}],"ears":"When a staff user opens a product, the portal shall return its imported stock quantity, stock status and its price on each price list.","id":"REQ-46","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-6","I-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order with delivery date Thursday","id":"AC-47.1","level":"api","then":"The Wednesday change response status is 200 and the Tuesday change response status is 422 with an error naming the deliveryDate field","when":"At Monday 15:00 staff change the date to Wednesday, then to Tuesday"},{"given":"A Received order of company A","id":"AC-47.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 and the order's address value is unchanged","when":"Staff change the delivery address to an address of company B"},{"given":"A Confirmed order","id":"AC-47.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 and the line quantity value is unchanged","when":"Staff change a line quantity"}],"ears":"While an order is in Received status, the portal shall let staff change line quantities, remove lines, change the note, change the delivery address to another address of the same company and change the delivery date to a date selectable at the time of the edit.","id":"REQ-47","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-4","Q-4","ASM-35"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order with 5 of X","id":"AC-48.1","level":"api","then":"An amendment record shows X 5 → 3 with the staff user and time, and one email naming X, 5 and 3 is sent to the order recipient","when":"Staff change the quantity of X to 3"},{"given":"A Received order","id":"AC-48.2","level":"api","then":"No email is sent","when":"Staff change only the delivery date and note"}],"ears":"When staff change a line quantity or remove a line on an order, the portal shall record the amendment with old and new quantity, staff user and time, and send an email describing the change.","id":"REQ-48","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-8","ASM-33","ASM-35"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order ORD-000124 where staff reduced X from 5 to 3","id":"AC-49.1","level":"api","then":"The status value is Confirmed, the last timeline entry names the staff user, and the email sent contains ORD-000124, the lines, the delivery date and address, and the change of X from 5 to 3","when":"Staff confirm it"},{"given":"A Received order with 5 of BP-100 while only 3 are in stock","id":"AC-49.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409, the error lists BP-100 and the status value stays Received","when":"Staff confirm it"}],"ears":"When staff confirm an order in Received status whose lines are all within available stock and whose delivery address still exists, the portal shall set the status to Confirmed, add a timeline entry with the staff user and time, and send a confirmation email with the order number, lines, delivery details and any staff quantity changes.","id":"REQ-49","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Confirmed order","id":"AC-50.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the last timeline entry has status Picking, the staff user and the time","when":"Staff set it to Picking"},{"given":"A Confirmed order","id":"AC-50.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 and the status value stays Confirmed","when":"Staff set it to Out for delivery"},{"given":"A Picking order","id":"AC-50.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409","when":"Staff set it back to Confirmed"},{"given":"A Picking order of a company that has been set inactive","id":"AC-50.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200","when":"Staff set it to Out for delivery"}],"ears":"When staff advance an order's status, the portal shall accept only the next status in the sequence Confirmed, Picking, Out for delivery, Delivered and add a timeline entry with the staff user and time.","id":"REQ-50","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","Q-3","Q-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Picking order ORD-000124","id":"AC-51.1","level":"api","then":"One email containing ORD-000124 and the text \"out for delivery\" is sent to the order recipient","when":"Staff set it to Out for delivery"}],"ears":"When an order's status changes to Out for delivery, the portal shall send an email identifying the order and stating it is out for delivery.","id":"REQ-51","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-14","ASM-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Out for delivery order","id":"AC-52.1","level":"api","then":"The status value is Cancelled, the timeline entry records the reason, staff user and time, and an email containing \"Customer closed\" is sent","when":"Staff cancel it with reason \"Customer closed\""},{"given":"A Received order","id":"AC-52.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 and the status value stays Received","when":"Staff reject it without a reason"},{"given":"A Delivered order","id":"AC-52.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 and the status value stays Delivered","when":"Staff cancel it with a reason"}],"ears":"When staff cancel or reject an order that is neither Delivered nor Cancelled, the portal shall require a reason, set the status to Cancelled, record the reason, staff user and time, and send a cancellation email containing the reason.","id":"REQ-52","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","Q-3","ASM-16","ASM-34"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active company A on price list Workshop A","id":"AC-53.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201, the order has status Received, the line unit price comes from Workshop A and the createdBy field names the staff user","when":"A staff user submits an order for company A with 2 of X and a valid address and date"},{"given":"The order from AC-53.1","id":"AC-53.2","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains the order","when":"A Buyer of company A lists orders"}],"ears":"When staff submit an order on behalf of an active customer company, the portal shall create it in Received status under the same price, stock, address and delivery-date rules as a Buyer order, marked as created by that staff user.","id":"REQ-53","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","I-14","ASM-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"For 8 Oct: 2 Confirmed orders and 1 Cancelled order; for 9 Oct: 1 order","id":"AC-54.1","level":"api","then":"The returned file is CSV with a header row and 2 data rows, each with the listed columns","when":"Staff export the delivery list for 8 Oct"},{"given":"An order for today","id":"AC-54.2","level":"api","then":"The returned file contains that order","when":"Staff export the delivery list without a date"}],"ears":"When staff export the delivery list for a date (default today), the portal shall return a CSV file with one row per non-Cancelled order whose requested delivery date is that date, containing order number, customer name, delivery address, address contact name and phone, delivery date, line summary, order note and status.","id":"REQ-54","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","ASM-27"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"3 Received orders, 1 Picking, 2 Out for delivery, 2 non-Cancelled orders due today, 4 Unpaid and 1 Overdue invoice, and 1 failed import after the last success","id":"AC-55.1","level":"api","then":"The returned count fields are 3, 1, 2, 2, 4, 1 and 1 respectively","when":"A staff user requests the dashboard"}],"ears":"When a staff user opens the dashboard, the portal shall return counts of orders in Received, Picking and Out for delivery status, non-Cancelled orders due for delivery today, Unpaid and Overdue invoices, and failed stock imports since the last successful import.","id":"REQ-55","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Out for delivery order with net total 100.00, tax rate 20% and last invoice INV-000049","id":"AC-56.1","level":"api","then":"One invoice record exists with number INV-000050, net 100.00, tax 20.00, gross 120.00 and status Unpaid","when":"Staff set it to Delivered"},{"given":"An Out for delivery order of an inactive company","id":"AC-56.2","level":"api","then":"One invoice record is created for that order","when":"Staff set it to Delivered"},{"given":"A Picking order","id":"AC-56.3","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains no invoice for that order","when":"The Buyer lists invoices"}],"ears":"When an order's status becomes Delivered, the portal shall create one invoice for it with the next sequential prefixed invoice number, the company's billing address, the order number, the invoice date, the order lines at order-time prices, the net total, tax at the configured rate, the gross total and payment status Unpaid.","id":"REQ-56","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","I-5","Q-8","ASM-2","ASM-9","ASM-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A has 2 invoices for orders placed by different Buyers, company B has 1","id":"AC-57.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list has 2 rows with the listed fields","when":"Buyer A1 lists invoices"},{"given":"The same invoices","id":"AC-57.2","level":"api","then":"The returned list has 3 rows","when":"A staff user lists invoices"}],"ears":"When a user lists invoices, the portal shall return invoice number, order number, invoice date, gross total and payment status for every invoice of the Buyer's own company, or of all companies for staff.","id":"REQ-57","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-16","Q-2","ASM-32"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Invoice INV-000050 for ORD-000124 with gross 120.00","id":"AC-58.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, the content type is application/pdf and the text extracted from the file contains INV-000050, ORD-000124 and 120.00","when":"A Buyer of that company downloads it"},{"given":"The same invoice","id":"AC-58.2","level":"manual","then":"The logo and company details from settings are displayed in the header","when":"A person opens the downloaded PDF"}],"ears":"When a Buyer of the invoice's company or a staff user downloads an invoice, the portal shall return a PDF file containing the invoice number, invoice date, customer, billing address, order number, lines with quantities and prices, net, tax and gross totals, payment status, and the distributor's logo and company details from settings.","id":"REQ-58","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","I-5","ASM-26"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Overdue days 30 and an unpaid invoice dated 1 March","id":"AC-59.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned values are Unpaid and Overdue","when":"The invoice-status calculator's public method is called for 31 March and for 1 April"},{"given":"An invoice dated 1 January that is marked paid","id":"AC-59.2","level":"unit","then":"The returned value is Paid","when":"The invoice-status calculator is called for 1 April"}],"ears":"The portal shall report an unpaid invoice's payment status as Overdue once more than the configured number of days have passed since its invoice date, as Unpaid before that, and as Paid once payment is recorded.","id":"REQ-59","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","ASM-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Unpaid invoice","id":"AC-60.1","level":"api","then":"The invoice record has status Paid, payment date 6 Oct 2026 and recordedBy the staff user","when":"A staff user marks it paid with payment date 6 Oct 2026"},{"given":"An Unpaid invoice","id":"AC-60.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 and the status value stays Unpaid","when":"A staff user marks it paid without a payment date"},{"given":"A signed-in Buyer","id":"AC-60.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403","when":"The Buyer tries to mark an invoice of their company paid"}],"ears":"When staff mark an Unpaid or Overdue invoice as paid with a payment date, the portal shall set its status to Paid and record the payment date and the staff user.","id":"REQ-60","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Administrator","id":"AC-61.1","level":"api","then":"The create response status is 201 and the returned search list contains Wiper Blade","when":"The administrator creates product \"Wiper Blade\" with code WB-55 and a Buyer searches \"wiper\""},{"given":"Product WB-55 exists","id":"AC-61.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409","when":"The administrator creates another product with code WB-55"},{"given":"Product WB-55 is on an existing order","id":"AC-61.3","level":"api","then":"Buyer search no longer returns WB-55 and the existing order detail still returns its line","when":"The administrator retires WB-55"}],"ears":"The portal shall let administrators add, edit and retire products with name, internal product ID, manufacturer part number, unique distributor product code, description, category, manufacturer, unit of sale and pack size.","id":"REQ-61","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Administrator","id":"AC-62.1","level":"api","then":"The returned category list contains Lighting and a Buyer catalogue filtered by Lighting returns X","when":"The administrator creates category \"Lighting\" and assigns product X to it"},{"given":"Category Lighting","id":"AC-62.2","level":"api","then":"The returned category list does not contain Lighting","when":"The administrator retires it and a Buyer lists categories"}],"ears":"The portal shall let administrators create, rename and retire single-level categories and assign each product to one category.","id":"REQ-62","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-17","ASM-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product X with an existing image","id":"AC-63.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the product's returned imageUrl value points to the new image","when":"The administrator uploads a 2 MB PNG"},{"given":"Product X","id":"AC-63.2","level":"api","then":"Both responses have status 422 with an error naming the size or type and the imageUrl value is unchanged","when":"The administrator uploads an 11 MB JPEG and then a GIF"}],"ears":"When an administrator uploads a product image, the portal shall store it as the product's image, replacing any previous image, only if it is a JPEG, PNG or WebP file of at most 10 MB.","id":"REQ-63","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-29"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P with no compatibility entries","id":"AC-64.1","level":"api","then":"The product's returned compatibility list has 2 entries","when":"The administrator adds 3 entries and removes 1"}],"ears":"The portal shall let administrators add and remove vehicle compatibility entries of make, model, model year range, engine, fuel type and variant on a product, with any number of entries per product.","id":"REQ-64","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10","I-17","ASM-23"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A company with account number C-1001 exists","id":"AC-65.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409","when":"The administrator creates another company with C-1001"},{"given":"Active company A with 2 orders","id":"AC-65.2","level":"api","then":"The company status value is inactive and the returned list still contains the 2 orders","when":"The administrator sets company A inactive and a staff user lists orders for company A"}],"ears":"The portal shall let administrators create and edit customer companies with name, unique account number, primary contact, contact email, contact phone, billing address, assigned price list and active or inactive status.","id":"REQ-65","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-11","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A","id":"AC-66.1","level":"api","then":"The create response status is 201 and the returned address list contains Depot 2","when":"A staff user adds address \"Depot 2\" and a Buyer of company A lists addresses"},{"given":"A signed-in Buyer","id":"AC-66.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403","when":"The Buyer POSTs a new address for their company"},{"given":"Order ORD-000124 delivered to address Depot 2","id":"AC-66.3","level":"api","then":"The returned order delivery address still shows the Depot 2 details","when":"Staff remove Depot 2 and the order is opened"}],"ears":"The portal shall let staff and administrators add, edit and remove a customer company's delivery addresses, each with label, address lines 1 and 2, city, region, postal code, country, contact person and contact phone.","id":"REQ-66","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-13","Q-7","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Cutoff 14:00","id":"AC-67.1","level":"api","then":"The first returned date is Wednesday","when":"The administrator changes the cutoff to 12:00 and a Buyer requests delivery dates at Monday 12:30"},{"given":"A signed-in Office Staff user","id":"AC-67.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and the tax rate value is unchanged","when":"The user changes the tax rate"}],"ears":"The portal shall let administrators view and change the order cutoff time, system timezone, non-working dates, maximum delivery days ahead, low-stock threshold, overdue days, tax rate, order and invoice number prefixes, reset and invitation link validity, and the company details and logo used on invoices.","id":"REQ-67","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-5","ASM-8","ASM-11","ASM-36"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"In October: 2 delivered orders with 3 and 2 of X at 10.00 for companies A and B, and 1 cancelled order with 5 of X","id":"AC-68.1","level":"api","then":"The returned product list shows X with quantity 5 and net 50.00, and the customer list shows A 30.00 and B 20.00","when":"A staff user requests the report for 1–31 October"},{"given":"The same data","id":"AC-68.2","level":"api","then":"The returned file is CSV with the same values","when":"The staff user requests the CSV export"}],"ears":"When a staff user requests the sales report for a date range, the portal shall return, for orders delivered in that range, the quantity and net sales value per product and the net sales value per customer, both as an on-screen list and as a CSV file.","id":"REQ-68","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","ASM-20"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product X created by admin1","id":"AC-69.1","level":"api","then":"The returned createdBy value is admin1, lastChangedBy is admin2 and lastChangedAt equals the edit time","when":"admin2 edits the product description and an administrator opens product X"},{"given":"Price list Fleet created by admin1","id":"AC-69.2","level":"api","then":"The returned lastChangedBy value is admin1 with the change time","when":"admin1 changes a price on Fleet and an administrator opens Fleet"}],"ears":"The portal shall store on every order, invoice, customer company, user, product, category and price list record who created it and when and who last changed it and when, and return these fields to administrators.","id":"REQ-69","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","ASM-21"]}],"suggestions":["Confirm whether a Buyer's own cancellation and invoice creation should send emails (ASM-18 leaves this open).","Add date and status filters to the Buyer order history (request section 18 calls them recommended).","Decide what happens to companies still assigned to a price list when that list is deactivated.","Add a password strength policy for reset and invitation password setting.","Add a vehicle make/model/year lookup endpoint so the vehicle search form can offer dropdowns.","Consider WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility as an NFR.","Consider overdue-invoice reminder emails and a CSV import for vehicle compatibility in a later release.","Revisit the Customer Account Manager role and saved basket templates for release 2.","Confirm the exact staff dashboard widgets with management."]},{"assumptions":["There is no existing code, so every requirement is ADDED. Endpoint paths in the acceptance criteria only show the contract; the build can choose other names as long as the behaviour stays the same.","ASM-24 (Stripe card payments) contradicts the request, which says the portal takes no online card payments in this phase. This spec follows the request: staff only record that an invoice is paid, with a payment date and the user who recorded it (REQ-51).","ASM-21 limits audit to created/last-changed fields. The request also explicitly asks for an order status timeline and a record of order amendments, so both are kept (REQ-30, REQ-36).","When a whole ERP file fails validation (unreadable, missing a required column, or a non-numeric or negative quantity), none of it is applied. Only unknown product identifiers are skipped row by row (ASM-6).","A Buyer can repeat any order of their company, whatever its status (Q-6 does not limit which statuses count as eligible).","Staff removing an order line counts as a quantity change to 0, so it triggers the amendment email (ASM-35).","Product image formats are limited to JPEG, PNG and WebP. ASM-29 sets only the 10 MB limit.","Office Staff and Administrators both manage customer companies and their delivery addresses (Q-7, ASM-28).","Buyer order history can be filtered by status and order date range. The request recommends filters but leaves the details open.","The order email recipient is the Buyer who placed the order, or the company's contact email for staff-created orders (ASM-33).","Sessions time out after 60 minutes idle (NFR-6). The request asks for session management but gives no number."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"p95 response time ≤ 1.0 s for GET /catalogue with 50,000 products and 100 concurrent users","text":"Catalogue text, category and vehicle searches return results without noticeable delay for a catalogue of 50,000 active products."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"p95 response time ≤ 2.0 s at 200 concurrent users","text":"Order, basket, checkout and invoice endpoints respond within a set limit under normal load."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"0 cross-company records returned in an automated authorization test suite covering 100% of Buyer-facing endpoints","text":"Customer data stays separate between customer companies."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"Argon2id or bcrypt with cost ≥ 12; 0 plaintext or reversibly encrypted passwords in storage or logs","text":"Passwords are stored only as salted one-way hashes."},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"100% of endpoints served over HTTPS with TLS 1.2 or higher; HTTP requests redirected","text":"All traffic is encrypted in transit."},{"id":"NFR-6","metric":"Sessions invalidated after 60 minutes of inactivity","text":"Idle sessions expire."},{"id":"NFR-7","metric":"0 write calls from the portal to ERP systems or the ERP drop location (other than moving processed files)","text":"The portal treats ERP stock as read-only."},{"id":"NFR-8","metric":"A 50,000-row CSV imports in ≤ 10 minutes","text":"The nightly stock import finishes before business hours."},{"id":"NFR-9","metric":"≥ 99% of order and reset emails handed to the email service within 5 minutes of the triggering event","text":"Transactional emails go out soon after the event that triggers them."},{"id":"NFR-10","metric":"p95 PDF generation ≤ 5 s for invoices of up to 200 lines","text":"Invoice PDFs are generated on request within a set limit."},{"id":"NFR-11","metric":"All Buyer pages usable without horizontal scrolling at viewport widths from 360 px to 1920 px on the latest 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari","text":"The portal is a responsive web app on desktop and mobile browsers."},{"id":"NFR-12","metric":"≥ 99.5% monthly availability, measured outside announced maintenance windows","text":"The portal is available during business use."}],"outOfScope":["Customer Account Manager role (Q-1)","Saved basket templates, section 16 (ASM-1)","Buyers creating or editing delivery addresses (Q-7, ASM-13)","Backorders and ordering beyond imported stock (excluded in the request, section 8; ASM-4)","Online card payments and payment-method capture (the request says no online card payments in this phase, section 32)","Writing stock or orders back to the ERP (request section 9)","Route planning for deliveries (request section 22)","SMS and push notifications (ASM-17, ASM-18)","Full field-level audit trail beyond created/last-changed fields, status timelines and order amendments (ASM-21)","Migrating existing customer, product, price or vehicle data; the system starts empty with seed data (ASM-22)","Custom report builder (ASM-20)","Nested categories (ASM-15)","Basket persistence across sessions (ASM-14)","Volume, promotional, discount and date-effective pricing (request section 10: one price per product per price list)","Bulk CSV upload of vehicle compatibility data (ASM-23)","Languages other than English (ASM-10)","Native mobile apps (ASM-30)","Reproducing an existing client invoice template (ASM-26)"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active Buyer account buyer@a.test with password 'Correct#Pass1'","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response contains a session token and the role value 'Buyer'","when":"POST /auth/sign-in is called with those credentials"},{"given":"An active account buyer@a.test","id":"AC-1.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401, the error message is 'Invalid email or password', and no session token is returned","when":"POST /auth/sign-in is called with a wrong password"},{"given":"No account exists for nobody@x.test","id":"AC-1.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401 and the error message is the same 'Invalid email or password' text as AC-1.2","when":"POST /auth/sign-in is called with that email"},{"given":"No session token","id":"AC-1.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401","when":"GET /orders is called"}],"ears":"When a user submits an email address and password that match an active account, the portal shall start an authenticated session and return the user's role.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-1","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active account with 4 consecutive failed sign-ins","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"Both responses have status 423 and the error message states the account is temporarily locked","when":"A 5th sign-in with a wrong password is made and then, 1 minute later, a sign-in with the correct password is made"},{"given":"An account locked 15 minutes and 1 second ago","id":"AC-2.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and a session token is returned","when":"POST /auth/sign-in is called with the correct password"},{"given":"An account with 4 failed sign-ins followed by 1 successful sign-in","id":"AC-2.3","level":"api","then":"Each response status is 401 (not 423) and the account record lock field is empty","when":"4 more sign-ins with a wrong password are made"}],"ears":"If an account has 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts, then the portal shall lock that account for 15 minutes and reject every sign-in attempt during the lock with a temporary-lock error.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-37"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A deactivated Buyer with a correct password","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and the error message states the account is inactive","when":"POST /auth/sign-in is called"},{"given":"An active Buyer whose customer company has been set inactive","id":"AC-3.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and no session token is returned","when":"POST /auth/sign-in is called with correct credentials"},{"given":"A Buyer holding a valid session who is then deactivated by an administrator","id":"AC-3.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401 and the order count for the company is unchanged","when":"POST /orders is called with that session and a valid basket"}],"ears":"If a user is deactivated or belongs to an inactive customer company, then the portal shall reject that user's sign-in attempts and every request made with that user's existing sessions.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An account exists for buyer@a.test","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 202 and one email is sent to buyer@a.test containing a reset link","when":"POST /auth/password-reset is called with buyer@a.test"},{"given":"No account exists for nobody@x.test","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 202 with the same response body as AC-4.1 and no email is sent","when":"POST /auth/password-reset is called with nobody@x.test"}],"ears":"When a password reset is requested for the email address of an existing account, the portal shall send a reset email containing a single-use link valid for the configured period (default 1 hour).","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-19","ASM-18"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A reset link issued 10 minutes ago","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"The confirm response status is 200, sign-in with the new password returns status 200, and sign-in with the old password returns status 401","when":"POST /auth/password-reset/confirm is called with the link token and new password 'New#Pass2024', then sign-in is attempted with the new and old passwords"},{"given":"A reset link issued 61 minutes ago with default settings","id":"AC-5.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 410 and the error message states the link has expired","when":"POST /auth/password-reset/confirm is called with it"},{"given":"A reset link that has already been used once","id":"AC-5.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 410","when":"POST /auth/password-reset/confirm is called with it again"},{"given":"An account locked by 5 failed sign-ins and a reset link requested during the lock","id":"AC-5.4","level":"api","then":"The sign-in response status is 200","when":"The reset is confirmed and sign-in is attempted with the new password within the 15-minute lock"}],"ears":"When a user submits a new password with an unexpired, unused reset link, the portal shall replace the password, invalidate the link, and clear any sign-in lock on the account.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Buyer with a valid session token","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"The sign-out response status is 204 and the GET /orders response status is 401","when":"POST /auth/sign-out is called and then GET /orders is called with the same token"}],"ears":"When a signed-in user signs out, the portal shall invalidate that session.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An administrator session and customer company 'Workshop A'","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201, a user row exists with status 'Pending', and one invitation email is sent to new@a.test","when":"POST /admin/invitations is called with email new@a.test, role Buyer and company Workshop A"},{"given":"An invitation sent 2 days ago","id":"AC-7.2","level":"api","then":"The user row status is 'Active' and the sign-in response status is 200","when":"The invitee calls POST /invitations/accept with the token and password 'Set#Pass2024' and then signs in"},{"given":"An invitation sent 7 days and 1 minute ago","id":"AC-7.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 410 and the user row status remains 'Pending'","when":"POST /invitations/accept is called with its token"},{"given":"An expired pending invitation","id":"AC-7.4","level":"api","then":"A new invitation email is sent and the accept response status is 200","when":"The administrator calls POST /admin/invitations/{id}/resend and the invitee accepts using the new link"},{"given":"An administrator session","id":"AC-7.5","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 and the error names the missing company field","when":"POST /admin/invitations is called with role Buyer and no customer company"}],"ears":"When an administrator invites a user with the role Buyer (linked to a customer company) or Office Staff, the portal shall create a pending user and send an invitation email whose link is valid for the configured period (default 7 days).","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","Q-1","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer A of company A and order ORD-000200 belonging to company B","id":"AC-8.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 404 and no order data is returned","when":"Buyer A calls GET /orders/ORD-000200"},{"given":"Buyer A of company A and invoice INV-000050 belonging to company B","id":"AC-8.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 404","when":"Buyer A calls GET /invoices/INV-000050/pdf"},{"given":"Company A has 3 orders (2 placed by Buyer A, 1 by colleague Buyer A2) and company B has 2 orders","id":"AC-8.3","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains exactly the 3 company A orders","when":"Buyer A calls GET /orders"},{"given":"Buyer A of company A","id":"AC-8.4","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains only company A's delivery addresses","when":"Buyer A calls GET /addresses"}],"ears":"The portal shall restrict each Buyer to the orders, invoices, prices, delivery addresses and account data of the Buyer's own customer company.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-5","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Buyer session","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403","when":"GET /staff/orders is called"},{"given":"An Office Staff session","id":"AC-9.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and no product row is created","when":"POST /admin/products is called with a valid product"},{"given":"An Administrator session and an order in status Received","id":"AC-9.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the order status field is 'Confirmed'","when":"POST /staff/orders/{id}/confirm is called"}],"ears":"The portal shall allow Office Staff functions only to Office Staff and Administrator users and administration functions only to Administrator users.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-6","I-17","ASM-28","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active product 'Front Brake Pad Set', code 'BP-1001', part number 'MPN-77A', brand 'Brembo', and retired product 'Brake Pad Old', code 'BP-0001'","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains BP-1001 and does not contain BP-0001","when":"GET /catalogue?q=pad is called by a Buyer"},{"given":"The products from AC-10.1","id":"AC-10.2","level":"api","then":"Each returned list contains BP-1001","when":"GET /catalogue is called with q=1001, then q=mpn-77, then q=BREM"},{"given":"The products from AC-10.1","id":"AC-10.3","level":"api","then":"The returned list is empty and the response status is 200","when":"GET /catalogue?q=zzzz is called"}],"ears":"When a Buyer searches the catalogue with a text query, the portal shall return the active products whose name, distributor product code, manufacturer part number or manufacturer/brand contains the query as a case-insensitive partial match.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"3 active products in 'Filters' and 2 in 'Brake system'","id":"AC-11.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list count is 3 and every returned product has category 'Filters'","when":"GET /catalogue?category=Filters is called"},{"given":"The products from AC-11.1","id":"AC-11.2","level":"api","then":"The returned list count is 5","when":"GET /catalogue is called with no category parameter"}],"ears":"When a Buyer filters the catalogue by a category, the portal shall return only active products assigned to that category.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10","ASM-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P1 compatible with Ford Focus 2018 1.0 EcoBoost Petrol, and product P2 compatible with Ford Focus 2018 2.0 TDCi Diesel","id":"AC-12.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains P1 and P2","when":"GET /catalogue?make=Ford&model=Focus&year=2018 is called"},{"given":"The products from AC-12.1","id":"AC-12.2","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains P2 only","when":"GET /catalogue?make=Ford&model=Focus&year=2018&fuel=Diesel is called"}],"ears":"When a Buyer searches by vehicle make, model and year, optionally narrowed by engine, fuel type and variant, the portal shall return only active products that have a compatibility record matching every supplied value.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10","ASM-23"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active product with all fields populated and a price on the Buyer's price list","id":"AC-13.1","level":"api","then":"Each returned list item contains the fields imageUrl, name, productCode, manufacturer, unit, packSize, price and stockStatus with the product's values","when":"GET /catalogue is called by the Buyer"}],"ears":"The portal shall return, for each product in a Buyer's catalogue list, the image URL, name, distributor product code, manufacturer, unit of sale, pack size, the price for the Buyer's company and the stock status.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active product compatible with 2 vehicles","id":"AC-14.1","level":"api","then":"The response contains the listed fields and a compatibleVehicles list of count 2","when":"GET /catalogue/products/{id} is called by a Buyer"},{"given":"An active product with stock quantity 0","id":"AC-14.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the stockStatus value is 'Out of stock'","when":"GET /catalogue/products/{id} is called"}],"ears":"When a Buyer opens a product, the portal shall return the image URL, name, product code, manufacturer, description, unit, pack size, the price for the Buyer's company, stock status and the list of compatible vehicles.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product BP-1001 priced 15.00 on 'Standard' and 12.50 on 'Workshop A'; company A assigned 'Workshop A' and company B assigned 'Standard'","id":"AC-15.1","level":"api","then":"The price value returned to company A's Buyer is 12.50 and to company B's Buyer is 15.00","when":"A Buyer of company A and a Buyer of company B each call GET /catalogue/products/BP-1001"},{"given":"The data from AC-15.1 and an Office Staff session","id":"AC-15.2","level":"api","then":"The returned price value is 12.50","when":"GET /staff/customers/A/prices?product=BP-1001 is called"}],"ears":"The portal shall price every product shown to a customer company, or to staff acting for that company, at the product's price on the price list assigned to that company.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P3 is active but absent from company A's price list","id":"AC-16.1","level":"api","then":"The response price value is null and the priceStatus field is 'Price on request'","when":"A Buyer of company A calls GET /catalogue/products/P3"},{"given":"The data from AC-16.1","id":"AC-16.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422, the error states the product has no price, and the basket list does not contain P3","when":"POST /basket/lines is called with P3 quantity 1"}],"ears":"If a product has no price on the price list assigned to the customer company, then the portal shall show the product as 'Price on request' and reject adding it to a basket or order.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-11","ASM-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The low-stock threshold setting is 10","id":"AC-17.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned values are 'Out of stock', 'Low stock', 'Low stock' and 'In stock' respectively","when":"The stock status calculation is called with quantities 0, 1, 10 and 11"}],"ears":"The portal shall set a product's stock status to 'Out of stock' when its imported quantity is 0, 'Low stock' when the quantity is between 1 and the configured low-stock threshold inclusive, and 'In stock' when the quantity is above the threshold.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-12","ASM-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Products BP-1001 (quantity 4) and FL-200 (quantity 0) and a valid CSV listing BP-1001=25 and FL-200=3 in the import folder, threshold 10","id":"AC-18.1","level":"job","then":"The BP-1001 row has quantity 25 and status 'In stock', the FL-200 row has quantity 3 and status 'Low stock', and an import log record has status 'Success' with an applied row count of 2","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"When the scheduled stock import finds a valid ERP CSV file in the configured location, the portal shall update each listed product's stock quantity and stock status and write an import log record with the outcome and row counts.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","I-3","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A CSV with 3 rows for existing products and 1 row for unknown identifier 'XX-999'","id":"AC-19.1","level":"job","then":"The 3 product rows have the new quantities, and the import log record has an applied row count of 3 and a skipped identifiers list containing 'XX-999'","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"If a valid ERP CSV file contains product identifiers that do not match any product, then the portal shall apply the matching rows, skip the unknown rows, and list each skipped identifier in the import log record.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","ASM-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"BP-1001 has quantity 25 and the import folder holds a CSV missing the quantity column","id":"AC-20.1","level":"job","then":"The BP-1001 row still has quantity 25 and an import log record has status 'Failed' with a reason naming the missing column","when":"The stock import job runs"},{"given":"A CSV in which one row has quantity 'abc'","id":"AC-20.2","level":"job","then":"No product quantity value changes and the import log record status is 'Failed'","when":"The stock import job runs"},{"given":"A failed import log record exists","id":"AC-20.3","level":"api","then":"The returned list includes the record with status 'Failed' and its reason","when":"An Office Staff user calls GET /staff/stock-imports"}],"ears":"If an ERP CSV file is unreadable, lacks a required column, or contains a non-numeric or negative quantity, then the portal shall leave all stock data unchanged and write a failed import log record with the reason, visible to Office Staff and Administrators.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product BP-1001 with imported quantity 5","id":"AC-21.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 and the error message states 5 are available","when":"A Buyer calls POST /basket/lines with BP-1001 quantity 6"},{"given":"Product FL-200 with imported quantity 0","id":"AC-21.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 and the basket list does not contain FL-200","when":"A Buyer calls POST /basket/lines with FL-200 quantity 1"},{"given":"Product BP-1001 with imported quantity 5","id":"AC-21.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the basket line quantity value is 5","when":"A Buyer calls POST /basket/lines with BP-1001 quantity 5"}],"ears":"If a basket line, order line or staff amendment would set a quantity above the product's imported stock quantity, or the product is Out of stock, then the portal shall reject the change with an error stating the available quantity.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-12","I-13","ASM-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An empty basket and company prices BP-1001=12.50 and FL-200=4.00 with enough stock","id":"AC-22.1","level":"api","then":"The response lists line totals 25.00 and 4.00 and a subtotal value of 29.00","when":"The Buyer adds BP-1001 quantity 2 and FL-200 quantity 1 and calls GET /basket"},{"given":"The basket from AC-22.1","id":"AC-22.2","level":"api","then":"The GET /basket response lists one line with line total 37.50 and subtotal 37.50","when":"The Buyer changes BP-1001 to quantity 3 and removes FL-200"},{"given":"The basket from AC-22.1","id":"AC-22.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 and the line quantity value stays 2","when":"PATCH /basket/lines/BP-1001 is called with quantity 0 or -1"},{"given":"A Buyer with a basket containing 2 lines","id":"AC-22.4","level":"api","then":"The returned basket list is empty","when":"The Buyer signs out, signs in again and calls GET /basket"}],"ears":"While a Buyer's session is active, the portal shall keep the Buyer's basket and return each line's unit price, quantity and line total (unit price × quantity) and the basket subtotal (sum of line totals) after each add, quantity change or removal.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-14","ASM-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A has addresses A1 and A2 and company B has address B1","id":"AC-23.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 and the basket delivery address field is unchanged","when":"A Buyer of company A calls PUT /basket/delivery with address B1"},{"given":"The data from AC-23.1","id":"AC-23.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the basket delivery address field is A2","when":"A Buyer of company A calls PUT /basket/delivery with address A2"}],"ears":"If an order or basket is given a delivery address that does not belong to the order's customer company, then the portal shall reject it with a validation error.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","Q-7","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Cutoff 14:00, Saturdays and Sundays configured as non-working, Monday 2026-10-05 is a working day","id":"AC-24.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned dates are Tuesday 2026-10-06, Wednesday 2026-10-07 and Wednesday 2026-10-07","when":"The delivery date calculator is called with Monday 13:00, Monday 14:00 and Monday 15:00"},{"given":"The settings from AC-24.1","id":"AC-24.2","level":"unit","then":"The returned dates are Monday 2026-10-12 and Tuesday 2026-10-13","when":"The calculator is called with Friday 2026-10-09 13:00 and Friday 2026-10-09 15:00"},{"given":"The settings from AC-24.1 plus Tuesday 2026-10-06 configured as a public holiday","id":"AC-24.3","level":"unit","then":"The returned date is Wednesday 2026-10-07","when":"The calculator is called with Monday 2026-10-05 13:00"},{"given":"Timezone Europe/London and an order instant of 13:30 UTC on Monday 2026-10-05 (14:30 local)","id":"AC-24.4","level":"unit","then":"The returned date is Wednesday 2026-10-07","when":"The calculator is called"}],"ears":"The portal shall calculate the earliest delivery date, in the configured timezone, as the next working day for orders placed before the configured cutoff (default 14:00) and as the working day after the next working day for orders placed at or after the cutoff, skipping configured non-working dates.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-11","ASM-36"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Now is Monday 2026-10-05 15:00, cutoff 14:00, maximum 30 days ahead","id":"AC-25.1","level":"api","then":"Each response status is 422 with an error naming the date rule broken","when":"PUT /basket/delivery is called with dates 2026-10-06, 2026-10-10 (Saturday) and 2026-11-20"},{"given":"The settings from AC-25.1","id":"AC-25.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the basket delivery date field is 2026-10-07","when":"PUT /basket/delivery is called with 2026-10-07"},{"given":"The settings from AC-25.1","id":"AC-25.3","level":"api","then":"The returned list starts at 2026-10-07, contains only working days and ends no later than 2026-11-04","when":"GET /delivery-dates is called"}],"ears":"If a delivery date chosen by a Buyer or staff user is earlier than the earliest delivery date, is a non-working date, or is more than the configured maximum number of days ahead, then the portal shall reject it with a validation error.","id":"REQ-25","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A basket with BP-1001 quantity 2 added at 12.50, after which the Workshop A price changed to 13.00","id":"AC-26.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409, the response lists BP-1001 with current price 13.00, and no order row is created","when":"POST /orders is called"},{"given":"A basket with FL-200 quantity 4, after which a stock import set FL-200 to quantity 2","id":"AC-26.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409, the response lists FL-200 with available quantity 2, and no order row is created","when":"POST /orders is called"},{"given":"A basket line whose product was retired after it was added","id":"AC-26.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 and the response lists the line as unavailable","when":"POST /orders is called"}],"ears":"When a Buyer submits checkout, the portal shall re-check every line's stock and current company price and, if any line is unavailable, over stock or re-priced, reject the submission with the list of affected lines and their current values.","id":"REQ-26","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A basket with 2 lines, an address, a delivery date and a note","id":"AC-27.1","level":"manual","then":"The page shows every listed value matching the basket, with the submit button below them","when":"A tester opens the checkout review page in a browser"}],"ears":"When a Buyer proceeds to the final checkout step, the portal shall display the order lines, quantities, unit prices, line totals, subtotal, delivery address, delivery date and order note before the submit action.","id":"REQ-27","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Order prefix 'ORD-', last order number ORD-000123, and a valid basket with BP-1001 ×2 at 12.50, address A1, date 2026-10-07 and note 'Rear door'","id":"AC-28.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201, the returned order number is ORD-000124, the status value is 'Received', the order row stores line unit price 12.50, address A1, date 2026-10-07 and note 'Rear door', and GET /basket returns an empty list","when":"POST /orders is called"},{"given":"The order from AC-28.1","id":"AC-28.2","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains ORD-000124","when":"An Office Staff user calls GET /staff/orders?status=Received"},{"given":"A valid basket with no note","id":"AC-28.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the order note field is empty","when":"POST /orders is called"}],"ears":"When a valid checkout is submitted, the portal shall create an order with the next sequential prefixed order number, status 'Received', the lines with order-time unit prices, the delivery address, delivery date and optional note, and shall empty the basket.","id":"REQ-28","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-4","I-13","ASM-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Order ORD-000124 with BP-1001 at 12.50","id":"AC-29.1","level":"api","then":"The returned line unit price is 12.50 and the order total value is unchanged","when":"An administrator sets BP-1001 to 14.00 on Workshop A and then reassigns company A to 'Standard', and the Buyer calls GET /orders/ORD-000124"}],"ears":"The portal shall keep the unit prices stored on an existing order unchanged when price lists or a company's price list assignment change.","id":"REQ-29","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An order placed by Buyer Ann and confirmed by staff user Sam","id":"AC-30.1","level":"api","then":"The returned timeline list has 2 entries: 'Received' by Ann and 'Confirmed' by Sam, each with a timestamp","when":"GET /orders/{id} is called"}],"ears":"When an order changes status, the portal shall append a timeline entry recording the new status, the date and time, and the user who made the change or 'System'.","id":"REQ-30","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","I-14","I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A has a Received order by Buyer Ann, a Delivered order by Buyer Ben and a staff-created Confirmed order","id":"AC-31.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list has count 3 and each item has orderNumber, orderDate, deliveryDate, deliveryAddress, total and status fields","when":"Ann calls GET /orders"},{"given":"The data from AC-31.1","id":"AC-31.2","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains only Ben's order","when":"Ann calls GET /orders?status=Delivered"}],"ears":"When a Buyer lists orders, the portal shall return every order of the Buyer's company, including staff-created orders, with order number, order date, delivery date, delivery address, total and status, filterable by status and order date range.","id":"REQ-31","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-15","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An order whose BP-1001 quantity was amended by staff from 4 to 2","id":"AC-32.1","level":"api","then":"The response contains all listed fields and an amendments list with an entry showing BP-1001 changed from 4 to 2, the staff user and the time","when":"The Buyer calls GET /orders/{id}"}],"ears":"When a Buyer or staff user opens an order, the portal shall return the order number, order date, customer, delivery address, requested delivery date, current status, status timeline, lines with quantities, unit prices and line totals, order total, order note, and any staff amendments.","id":"REQ-32","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order placed by colleague Ben","id":"AC-33.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, the order status value is 'Cancelled' and a timeline entry by Ann is recorded","when":"Buyer Ann of the same company calls POST /orders/{id}/cancel"},{"given":"A Confirmed order of Ann's company","id":"AC-33.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409, the error message says to contact the distributor office, and the status value stays 'Confirmed'","when":"Ann calls POST /orders/{id}/cancel"}],"ears":"When a Buyer cancels an order of the Buyer's company, the portal shall set the order to 'Cancelled' only if its status is 'Received' and otherwise reject the cancellation with an error telling the Buyer to contact the office.","id":"REQ-33","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A colleague's order with BP-1001 ×2 at 12.50 (now 13.00, stock 50) and FL-200 ×1 (now retired)","id":"AC-34.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, the basket list contains BP-1001 quantity 2 at 13.00, the response flags FL-200 as unavailable, and the company order count is unchanged","when":"The Buyer calls POST /orders/{id}/repeat"},{"given":"An order with BP-1001 ×10 where current stock is 6","id":"AC-34.2","level":"api","then":"The response flags BP-1001 with available quantity 6 and the basket line quantity value is not above 6","when":"The Buyer calls POST /orders/{id}/repeat"}],"ears":"When a Buyer repeats an order of the Buyer's company, the portal shall add its orderable lines to the Buyer's basket at current company prices and flag lines that are retired, out of stock or without a price, without creating an order.","id":"REQ-34","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15","Q-6","ASM-3","ASM-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"5 orders across companies A and B with mixed statuses","id":"AC-35.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains only company A orders in status Received, each with the listed fields","when":"Office Staff call GET /staff/orders?customer=A&status=Received"}],"ears":"When Office Staff open the order queue, the portal shall list all orders with order number, customer, order date, requested delivery date, order total and current status, filterable by customer, order date range and status.","id":"REQ-35","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-14","I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order with BP-1001 ×4","id":"AC-36.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and an amendment row records the line, old value 4, new value 2, the staff user and the time","when":"Office Staff call PATCH /staff/orders/{id} setting BP-1001 to 2"},{"given":"A Confirmed order","id":"AC-36.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 and the order row is unchanged","when":"Office Staff call PATCH /staff/orders/{id} with any change"},{"given":"A Received order placed Monday 13:00 with delivery Tuesday, edited on Monday 15:00","id":"AC-36.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 with an error naming the cutoff rule","when":"Office Staff call PATCH /staff/orders/{id} with delivery date Tuesday"},{"given":"A Received order of company A","id":"AC-36.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422","when":"Office Staff call PATCH /staff/orders/{id} with company B's address"}],"ears":"While an order is in status 'Received', the portal shall allow Office Staff to change line quantities, remove lines, change the delivery date (validated against the cutoff rule at the time of the edit), change the delivery address (to one of the company's addresses) and edit the note, recording each change as an amendment.","id":"REQ-36","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-4","Q-4","ASM-35"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order placed by Buyer Ann with BP-1001 ×4 and FL-200 ×1","id":"AC-37.1","level":"api","then":"An email is sent to Ann listing BP-1001 4→2 and FL-200 1→0","when":"Office Staff set BP-1001 to 2 and remove FL-200"},{"given":"A Received order","id":"AC-37.2","level":"api","then":"No email is sent","when":"Office Staff change only the delivery address"}],"ears":"When Office Staff change a line quantity or remove a line on a Received order, the portal shall send an email to the order's recipient listing each changed line with its old and new quantity.","id":"REQ-37","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-33","ASM-35","ASM-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order with all lines in stock","id":"AC-38.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, the status value is 'Confirmed', and the timeline entry records the staff user and time","when":"Office Staff call POST /staff/orders/{id}/confirm"},{"given":"A Received order with BP-1001 ×6 where stock is now 3","id":"AC-38.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409, the response lists BP-1001 with available quantity 3, and the status value stays 'Received'","when":"Office Staff call POST /staff/orders/{id}/confirm"},{"given":"An order in status Picking","id":"AC-38.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409","when":"POST /staff/orders/{id}/confirm is called"}],"ears":"When Office Staff confirm a Received order whose lines are all active and within imported stock, the portal shall set the status to 'Confirmed' and record the confirming user and time, and otherwise reject the confirmation listing the failing lines.","id":"REQ-38","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Order ORD-000124 placed by Buyer Ann with BP-1001 amended from 4 to 2","id":"AC-39.1","level":"api","then":"One email is sent to Ann containing 'ORD-000124', the lines, total, address, date, and the change BP-1001 4→2","when":"Office Staff confirm it"},{"given":"A staff-created order for company A whose contact email is office@a.test","id":"AC-39.2","level":"api","then":"The confirmation email is sent to office@a.test","when":"Office Staff confirm it"}],"ears":"When an order becomes 'Confirmed', the portal shall send a confirmation email to the order's recipient containing the order number, lines, quantities, order total, delivery address, delivery date and any staff quantity changes.","id":"REQ-39","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-5","ASM-33","ASM-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Confirmed order","id":"AC-40.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 and the status value stays 'Confirmed'","when":"POST /staff/orders/{id}/status is called with 'Out for delivery'"},{"given":"A Picking order","id":"AC-40.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409","when":"POST /staff/orders/{id}/status is called with 'Confirmed'"},{"given":"A Picking order","id":"AC-40.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the status value is 'Out for delivery'","when":"POST /staff/orders/{id}/status is called with 'Out for delivery'"}],"ears":"If Office Staff request a status change other than Confirmed→Picking, Picking→Out for delivery, Out for delivery→Delivered, or cancellation, then the portal shall reject it and leave the status unchanged.","id":"REQ-40","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Picking order ORD-000124 placed by Buyer Ann","id":"AC-41.1","level":"api","then":"One email is sent to Ann containing 'ORD-000124' and the text 'out for delivery'","when":"Office Staff set it to 'Out for delivery'"}],"ears":"When an order becomes 'Out for delivery', the portal shall send an email to the order's recipient that identifies the order number and states the order is out for delivery.","id":"REQ-41","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-14","ASM-33","ASM-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Picking order placed by Buyer Ann","id":"AC-42.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, the status value is 'Cancelled', the order row stores reason 'Supplier recall', the staff user and time, and an email containing 'Supplier recall' is sent to Ann","when":"Office Staff call POST /staff/orders/{id}/cancel with reason 'Supplier recall'"},{"given":"A Received order","id":"AC-42.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 and the status value stays 'Received'","when":"POST /staff/orders/{id}/cancel is called with an empty reason"},{"given":"A Delivered order","id":"AC-42.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 and the status value stays 'Delivered'","when":"POST /staff/orders/{id}/cancel is called with a reason"}],"ears":"When Office Staff reject or cancel an order that is not 'Delivered' or 'Cancelled' and supply a reason, the portal shall set the order to 'Cancelled', record the reason, user and time, and email the order's recipient with the reason.","id":"REQ-42","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","Q-3","ASM-16","ASM-34","ASM-33"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active company A on 'Workshop A' (BP-1001=12.50) and address A1","id":"AC-43.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201, the order row has status 'Received', unit price 12.50 and createdBy the staff user, and company A's Buyer sees it in the GET /orders list","when":"Office Staff call POST /staff/orders with company A, address A1, BP-1001 ×2 and a valid date"},{"given":"Inactive company C","id":"AC-43.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 with an error stating the company is inactive and no order row is created","when":"Office Staff call POST /staff/orders for company C"}],"ears":"When Office Staff submit an order on behalf of an active customer company, the portal shall create it under the same address, stock, price and delivery-date rules as a Buyer order, with status 'Received' and the staff user recorded as creator.","id":"REQ-43","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","I-14","Q-8","ASM-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"For 2026-10-07: 2 Confirmed orders and 1 Cancelled order; 1 order for 2026-10-08","id":"AC-44.1","level":"api","then":"The response content type is text/csv, the file has a header row and 2 data rows for the Confirmed orders with the listed columns","when":"GET /staff/delivery-list.csv?date=2026-10-07 is called"},{"given":"Today is 2026-10-07 with the data from AC-44.1","id":"AC-44.2","level":"api","then":"The file has the same 2 data rows","when":"GET /staff/delivery-list.csv is called with no date"}],"ears":"When Office Staff export the delivery list for a date (default today), the portal shall return a CSV file of all non-Cancelled orders with that requested delivery date, one row per order with order number, customer, delivery address, contact name and phone, delivery date, order lines summary, note and status.","id":"REQ-44","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","ASM-27"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"3 Received, 2 Picking, 1 Out for delivery orders, 2 non-cancelled orders due today, 4 Unpaid and 1 Overdue invoice, and 1 failed import yesterday","id":"AC-45.1","level":"api","then":"The response count fields are received=3, picking=2, outForDelivery=1, dueToday=2, unpaid=4, overdue=1, failedImports=1","when":"GET /staff/dashboard is called"}],"ears":"When Office Staff open the dashboard, the portal shall return the counts of Received orders, Picking orders, Out for delivery orders, orders due for delivery today, Unpaid and Overdue invoices, and failed stock imports in the last 7 days.","id":"REQ-45","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-7","I-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Companies 'Smith Motors' (ACC-1001) and 'Fleetline Ltd' (ACC-2002)","id":"AC-46.1","level":"api","then":"The first returned list contains only Smith Motors and the second only Fleetline Ltd","when":"Office Staff call GET /staff/customers?q=smith and then GET /staff/customers?q=2002"},{"given":"Company Smith Motors with 2 addresses and 3 users","id":"AC-46.2","level":"api","then":"The response contains the company fields, an addresses list of count 2, the price list name, a users list of count 3 and the status","when":"GET /staff/customers/{id} is called"}],"ears":"When Office Staff search customers by a partial company name or account number, the portal shall return the matching customer companies, and opening one shall return its details, addresses, assigned price list, users and status.","id":"REQ-46","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Invoice prefix 'INV-', last invoice INV-000050, tax rate 20%, and an Out for delivery order with net total 100.00","id":"AC-47.1","level":"api","then":"An invoice row INV-000051 exists for the order with net 100.00, tax rate 20%, tax 20.00, gross 120.00 and status 'Unpaid'","when":"Office Staff set it to 'Delivered'"},{"given":"An Out for delivery order of a company set inactive after the order was placed","id":"AC-47.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and an invoice row is created for the order","when":"Office Staff set it to 'Delivered'"},{"given":"A Picking order","id":"AC-47.3","level":"api","then":"The returned list is empty","when":"GET /staff/invoices?order={id} is called"}],"ears":"When an order becomes 'Delivered', the portal shall create one invoice with the next sequential prefixed invoice number, invoice date, customer, billing address, order number, the order's lines, quantities and order-time prices, net total, configured tax rate, tax amount, gross total and status 'Unpaid'.","id":"REQ-47","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","I-5","ASM-2","ASM-9","ASM-25","Q-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Overdue setting 30 days and today 2026-11-10","id":"AC-48.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned values are 'Overdue', 'Unpaid' and 'Paid'","when":"The invoice status calculation is called for unpaid invoices dated 2026-10-10 and 2026-10-11, and a paid invoice dated 2026-09-01"}],"ears":"The portal shall report an invoice as 'Overdue' when it is unpaid and more than the configured number of days have passed since the invoice date, as 'Unpaid' when it is unpaid within that period, and as 'Paid' once payment is recorded.","id":"REQ-48","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","ASM-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A has 2 invoices (one from a colleague's order) and company B has 1","id":"AC-49.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list has count 2 and each item has invoiceNumber, invoiceDate, orderNumber, grossTotal and status fields","when":"A Buyer of company A calls GET /invoices"}],"ears":"When a Buyer lists invoices, the portal shall return every invoice of the Buyer's company with invoice number, invoice date, order number, gross total and payment status.","id":"REQ-49","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-16","Q-2","ASM-32"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Invoice INV-000051 of company A","id":"AC-50.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, the content type is application/pdf, and the file text contains 'INV-000051', the order number, the billing address and the gross total 120.00","when":"A Buyer of company A calls GET /invoices/INV-000051/pdf"},{"given":"Invoice INV-000051","id":"AC-50.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the content type is application/pdf","when":"An Office Staff user calls GET /staff/invoices/INV-000051/pdf"}],"ears":"When a Buyer of the invoice's company or a staff user downloads an invoice, the portal shall return a PDF file containing the distributor logo and company details from settings, invoice number, invoice date, customer, billing address, order number, lines, quantities, prices, net, tax and gross totals, and payment status.","id":"REQ-50","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","I-5","ASM-26"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Unpaid invoice INV-000051","id":"AC-51.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the invoice row has status 'Paid', paymentDate 2026-10-20 and paymentRecordedBy the staff user","when":"Office Staff call POST /staff/invoices/INV-000051/payment with date 2026-10-20"},{"given":"Unpaid invoice INV-000051","id":"AC-51.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 and the status value stays 'Unpaid'","when":"POST /staff/invoices/INV-000051/payment is called without a date"},{"given":"A Buyer session","id":"AC-51.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403","when":"POST /staff/invoices/INV-000051/payment is called"}],"ears":"When Office Staff mark an unpaid invoice as paid with a payment date, the portal shall set its status to 'Paid' and record the payment date and the recording user.","id":"REQ-51","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Existing product code BP-1001","id":"AC-52.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 and the error names the duplicate product code","when":"An Administrator calls POST /admin/products with code BP-1001"},{"given":"Product BP-1001 appears on order ORD-000124","id":"AC-52.2","level":"api","then":"The catalogue list is empty and the order response still lists the BP-1001 line with its name and price","when":"An Administrator retires BP-1001 and a Buyer calls GET /catalogue?q=BP-1001 and GET /orders/ORD-000124"}],"ears":"The portal shall allow Administrators to add, edit and retire products with name, internal ID, unique distributor product code, manufacturer part number, description, category, manufacturer, unit of sale and pack size, keeping retired products out of the catalogue but on existing orders.","id":"REQ-52","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Administrator session","id":"AC-53.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the returned category list contains 'Exhaust'","when":"POST /admin/categories is called with name 'Exhaust' and then GET /catalogue/categories is called by a Buyer"},{"given":"Category 'Exhaust'","id":"AC-53.2","level":"api","then":"The returned category list does not contain 'Exhaust'","when":"An Administrator retires it and a Buyer calls GET /catalogue/categories"}],"ears":"The portal shall allow Administrators to create, edit and retire single-level categories and assign products to them, hiding retired categories from the Buyer category filter.","id":"REQ-53","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-10","ASM-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product BP-1001 with an existing image","id":"AC-54.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the product imageUrl value returned by GET /catalogue/products/BP-1001 points to the new file","when":"An Administrator uploads a 2 MB PNG to POST /admin/products/BP-1001/image"},{"given":"Product BP-1001","id":"AC-54.2","level":"api","then":"Both responses have status 422 with errors naming the size limit and the file type, and the imageUrl value is unchanged","when":"An Administrator uploads an 11 MB JPEG, then a 1 MB .exe file"}],"ears":"When an Administrator uploads a product image, the portal shall accept JPEG, PNG or WebP files of up to 10 MB, store them in cloud storage, and replace any previous image for that product.","id":"REQ-54","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-29"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P1 with no compatibility records","id":"AC-55.1","level":"api","then":"Both returned lists contain P1","when":"An Administrator adds Ford Focus 2018 and VW Golf 2019 and a Buyer searches by each vehicle"},{"given":"Product P1 compatible with VW Golf 2019","id":"AC-55.2","level":"api","then":"The returned list does not contain P1","when":"An Administrator removes that record and a Buyer searches for VW Golf 2019"}],"ears":"The portal shall allow Administrators to add and remove vehicle compatibility records (make, model, year, engine, fuel type, variant) for a product, with any number of records per product.","id":"REQ-55","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-10","I-2","ASM-23"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Price list 'Fleet' with BP-1001 at 11.00","id":"AC-56.1","level":"api","then":"The price list has exactly one BP-1001 row with value 11.50","when":"An Administrator sets BP-1001 to 11.50 on 'Fleet'"},{"given":"Company A assigned 'Workshop A'","id":"AC-56.2","level":"api","then":"The returned price value is 11.50","when":"An Administrator assigns 'Fleet' to company A and a Buyer of company A calls GET /catalogue/products/BP-1001"},{"given":"Deactivated price list 'Old Dealer'","id":"AC-56.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 and the company's price list field is unchanged","when":"An Administrator assigns it to company A"},{"given":"BP-1001 on 'Fleet'","id":"AC-56.4","level":"api","then":"The returned priceStatus value is 'Price on request'","when":"An Administrator removes BP-1001 from 'Fleet' and a Fleet company Buyer opens BP-1001"}],"ears":"The portal shall allow Administrators to create, rename and deactivate price lists, set, edit and remove one price per product per price list, and assign an active price list to a customer company.","id":"REQ-56","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Administrator session","id":"AC-57.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409","when":"POST /admin/customers is called with account number ACC-1001 that already exists"},{"given":"An Office Staff session and company A","id":"AC-57.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and company A's Buyer sees 'Depot 2' in the GET /addresses list","when":"POST /staff/customers/A/addresses is called with label 'Depot 2' and full address fields"},{"given":"A Buyer of company A","id":"AC-57.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and the address count is unchanged","when":"POST /addresses is called with a new address"}],"ears":"The portal shall allow Office Staff and Administrators to create and edit customer companies (name, unique account number, primary contact, contact email, contact phone, billing address, assigned price list, active status) and their delivery addresses, and shall deny address changes to Buyers.","id":"REQ-57","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","Q-7","ASM-13","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company C with a Confirmed order and a paid invoice, then set inactive","id":"AC-58.1","level":"api","then":"Both lists return the existing records and the status response is 200 with status value 'Picking'","when":"Office Staff call GET /staff/orders?customer=C, GET /staff/invoices?customer=C, and POST /staff/orders/{id}/status with 'Picking'"}],"ears":"While a customer company is inactive, the portal shall keep its existing orders and invoices visible to staff and allow staff to progress, cancel and invoice its open orders.","id":"REQ-58","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-5","Q-8","I-14","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer Ann who placed order ORD-000124","id":"AC-59.1","level":"api","then":"The deactivate response status is 200, Ann's user row status is 'Deactivated', and the order response is returned with placedBy Ann","when":"An Administrator calls POST /admin/users/{ann}/deactivate and Office Staff call GET /staff/orders/ORD-000124"},{"given":"Deactivated Ann","id":"AC-59.2","level":"api","then":"The sign-in response status is 200","when":"An Administrator calls POST /admin/users/{ann}/reactivate and Ann signs in"},{"given":"Office Staff user Sam","id":"AC-59.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201","when":"An Administrator changes Sam's role to Administrator and Sam calls POST /admin/categories"}],"ears":"The portal shall allow Administrators to list users with role, company and account status, deactivate and reactivate users, change a user's role, and link Buyers to a customer company, without deleting any order or invoice record of a deactivated user.","id":"REQ-59","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-9","I-8","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Cutoff 14:00","id":"AC-60.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list starts at Wednesday","when":"An Administrator sets the cutoff to 12:00 via PUT /admin/settings and GET /delivery-dates is called on Monday 13:00 (working week)"},{"given":"An Office Staff session","id":"AC-60.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and the settings values are unchanged","when":"PUT /admin/settings is called"}],"ears":"The portal shall allow Administrators to set the order cutoff time, timezone, non-working dates, maximum delivery days ahead, low-stock threshold, overdue days, tax rate, order and invoice number prefixes, reset and invitation link validity, and the distributor's invoice logo and company details.","id":"REQ-60","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-36","ASM-11","ASM-5","ASM-8","ASM-12","ASM-19","ASM-25","ASM-26"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product BP-1001 created by admin Alice","id":"AC-61.1","level":"api","then":"The response fields show createdBy Alice, lastChangedBy Bob and a lastChangedAt timestamp later than createdAt","when":"Admin Bob edits its description and calls GET /admin/products/BP-1001"},{"given":"Company A edited by Office Staff Sam","id":"AC-61.2","level":"api","then":"The response field lastChangedBy is Sam","when":"An Administrator calls GET /admin/customers/A"}],"ears":"The portal shall store, on every order, invoice, customer company, user, product, category and price list record, who created it and when, and who last changed it and when, and return these fields to Administrators.","id":"REQ-61","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","ASM-21"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"In October 2026: company A has orders of net 100.00 and 50.00 and a Cancelled order of 30.00; BP-1001 sold 6 units for 75.00","id":"AC-62.1","level":"api","then":"The response lists company A with order count 2 and net total 150.00, and BP-1001 with quantity 6 and net total 75.00","when":"GET /staff/reports/sales?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31 is called"},{"given":"The data from AC-62.1","id":"AC-62.2","level":"api","then":"The response content type is text/csv and the file contains rows with the same values","when":"GET /staff/reports/sales.csv with the same range is called"}],"ears":"When Office Staff or Administrators request the sales report for a date range, the portal shall return, from non-Cancelled orders in that range, order count and net total per customer and quantity sold and net total per product, as an on-screen list and as a CSV file.","id":"REQ-62","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","ASM-20"]}],"suggestions":["Add the Customer Account Manager role in a later release, once company-wide visibility for Buyers (Q-2) has been reviewed.","Add saved basket templates (section 16) in a later run, including whether they are shared within a company.","Decide what happens to companies whose assigned price list is deactivated: block deactivation while it is assigned, or show 'Price on request'.","Decide whether staff can remove the last line of a Received order or must cancel it instead.","Think about sending an email when a Buyer cancels an order and when an invoice is created (ASM-18 leaves this open).","Add WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility targets and backup/restore objectives (RPO/RTO) as NFRs once the client confirms them.","Get the ERP CSV column layout and the drop location (folder or SFTP) from the client before building the import (ASM-7).","Think about an admin CSV upload for vehicle compatibility data, given how much data there may be (ASM-23).","Think about a hold or reservation on stock between order submission and confirmation, since imported quantities only refresh nightly."]},{"assumptions":["ASM-24 assumed Stripe card payments, but request section 32 says the portal takes no online card payments in this phase. This spec follows the request: staff record payments by hand (payment date and recording user).","Management has no separate role. Managers use Office Staff or Administrator accounts to see the sales report.","The portal uses one currency set in system settings, with amounts to 2 decimal places.","If a company has no assigned price list, or its list is deactivated, every product shows 'Price on request' for that company.","Placing or confirming an order does not reduce the imported stock quantity. Nothing is reserved; the next import brings in fresh quantities.","The whole ERP CSV file is rejected if a row has a non-numeric or negative quantity, or if a required column is missing. Unknown product identifiers alone do not reject the file (ASM-6).","At checkout, a price change or a stock shortfall since the item was added rejects the order submission and returns the current values, so the Buyer can review them before submitting again.","Staff may change quantities, remove lines, change the note, and change the date and address on Received orders. Adding new lines is not in the requested list of edits.","The invoice date is the date the order became Delivered.","Reactivating a user is allowed only while the user's company is active (this is how 'where permitted' is read).","HTTP status codes and error codes in the acceptance criteria are examples. The rule that is fixed is the outcome: success or rejection, and no record change on rejection.","Allowed product image types are JPEG, PNG and WebP. ASM-29 sets only the 10 MB limit."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"p95 response time <= 1.0 s","text":"Catalogue search and filter responses are returned within the stated time with 50,000 active products and 50 concurrent users."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"p95 response time <= 2.0 s","text":"Basket, checkout, order and invoice list endpoints respond within the stated time at 100 concurrent users."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"import duration <= 10 minutes","text":"The nightly stock import finishes within the stated time for a 100,000-row CSV."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"99% of emails handed off within 2 minutes of the event","text":"Order and account emails are handed to the email service soon after the triggering event."},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"p95 generation time <= 5 s","text":"Invoice PDF downloads are generated within the stated time for invoices up to 200 lines."},{"id":"NFR-6","metric":">= 99.5% monthly uptime; maintenance <= 4 hours per month","text":"Portal availability excluding announced maintenance windows."},{"id":"NFR-7","metric":"Argon2id or bcrypt with cost >= 12; 0 plaintext passwords found in log scan","text":"Passwords are stored only as salted hashes and never written to logs."},{"id":"NFR-8","metric":"TLS 1.2 or higher on 100% of endpoints; AES-256 at rest","text":"All traffic is encrypted in transit and all personal and order data encrypted at rest."},{"id":"NFR-9","metric":"idle timeout 30 minutes; absolute lifetime 12 hours","text":"Sessions expire after inactivity and after a maximum lifetime."},{"id":"NFR-10","metric":">= 128 bits of entropy per token","text":"Password-reset and invitation tokens are unguessable and stored hashed."},{"id":"NFR-11","metric":"100% of Buyer endpoints covered; 0 cross-company records returned","text":"Company data isolation is verified by automated authorisation tests over every Buyer endpoint."},{"id":"NFR-12","metric":"all Buyer and staff screens usable at viewport widths 360-1920 px on the latest 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari (manual check)","text":"The responsive web app works on desktop and mobile browsers."},{"id":"NFR-13","metric":"daily backups; RPO <= 24 hours; RTO <= 8 hours","text":"Data backup and recovery within one cloud region in the client's account."}],"outOfScope":["Customer Account Manager role (Q-1)","Saved basket templates, request section 16 (ASM-1)","Backorders and ordering above imported stock (request section 8; ASM-4)","Online card payments and any payment-provider integration (request section 32 says no online card payments in this phase; overrides ASM-24)","Partial payments and payment method capture","Customers creating or editing their own delivery addresses (Q-7, ASM-13)","A separate Rejected order status (ASM-16)","SMS and push notifications (ASM-17, ASM-18)","Full field-level audit trail beyond created/last-changed by and when (ASM-21)","Migration of existing customer, product, price or vehicle data (ASM-22)","CSV upload of vehicle compatibility data (ASM-23)","Nested categories (ASM-15)","Volume pricing, promotional pricing, discounts and price effective dates (request section 10: one price per product per price list)","Basket persistence across sessions (ASM-14)","Route planning (request section 22)","Custom report builder (ASM-20)","Native mobile apps (ASM-30)","Languages other than English (ASM-10)","Writing stock data back to the ERP (request section 9)"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active Buyer account buyer@acme.test with password 'Correct#1' linked to active company Acme Garage","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response contains a session token and the role value 'Buyer'","when":"POST /auth/sign-in is called with those credentials"}],"ears":"When a user submits an email address and password that match an active account, the portal shall create an authenticated session for that user.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"No account exists for nobody@acme.test","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401 and the error message is 'Invalid email or password'","when":"POST /auth/sign-in is called with nobody@acme.test and any password"},{"given":"An active account buyer@acme.test","id":"AC-2.2","level":"api","then":"The response status and error message are identical to AC-2.1 and no session token is returned","when":"POST /auth/sign-in is called with buyer@acme.test and a wrong password"}],"ears":"If a sign-in attempt uses an unknown email address or a wrong password, then the portal shall return the same invalid-credentials error for both cases.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active account that has just had 5 consecutive wrong-password attempts","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 423 with error code ACCOUNT_LOCKED and the message says the account is temporarily locked","when":"POST /auth/sign-in is called 1 minute later with the correct password"},{"given":"The same account, 15 minutes and 1 second after the fifth failure","id":"AC-3.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and a session token is returned","when":"POST /auth/sign-in is called with the correct password"},{"given":"An account with 4 wrong attempts, then 1 successful sign-in, then 4 more wrong attempts","id":"AC-3.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, showing the failure count was reset by the successful sign-in","when":"POST /auth/sign-in is called with the correct password"}],"ears":"If an account reaches 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts, then the portal shall block every sign-in attempt for that account for 15 minutes from the fifth failure.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-37"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active account buyer@acme.test","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and one email is sent to buyer@acme.test containing a reset link","when":"POST /auth/password-reset is called with buyer@acme.test"},{"given":"No account exists for nobody@acme.test","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"The response status and body are identical to AC-4.1 and no email is sent","when":"POST /auth/password-reset is called with nobody@acme.test"}],"ears":"When a user requests a password reset for a registered email address, the portal shall send a reset email containing a single-use link valid for the configured reset period (default 1 hour).","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-19","ASM-18"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A reset link issued 10 minutes ago for buyer@acme.test","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"The reset response status is 200, sign-in with 'NewPass#2' returns status 200 and sign-in with the old password returns status 401","when":"The new password 'NewPass#2' is submitted with that link and then sign-in is attempted"},{"given":"An account currently locked after 5 failed attempts and a valid reset link for it","id":"AC-5.2","level":"api","then":"The sign-in response status is 200","when":"A new password is submitted with the link and sign-in with the new password is attempted within the original 15-minute lock"}],"ears":"When a user submits a new password with an unexpired, unused reset link, the portal shall replace the account password and clear any active lockout on that account.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A reset link issued 61 minutes ago with the default 1-hour period","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 with error code LINK_EXPIRED and sign-in with the old password still returns status 200","when":"A new password is submitted with that link"},{"given":"A reset link that was already used successfully","id":"AC-6.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 with error code LINK_USED","when":"Another new password is submitted with the same link"}],"ears":"If a reset link is expired or has already been used, then the portal shall reject the password change and keep the existing password.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Buyer with a valid session token","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"The sign-out response status is 200 and the GET /orders response status is 401","when":"POST /auth/sign-out is called and then GET /orders is called with the same token"}],"ears":"When a signed-in user signs out, the portal shall invalidate that user's session token.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"No session token","id":"AC-8.1","level":"api","then":"Each response status is 401 and each response body contains no product, order or invoice fields","when":"GET /catalogue/products, GET /orders and GET /invoices are called"}],"ears":"If a request to any endpoint other than sign-in, password reset and invitation acceptance has no valid session, then the portal shall return status 401 without any record data.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Buyer","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403","when":"GET /staff/orders is called"},{"given":"A signed-in Office Staff user","id":"AC-9.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and no price list row is created","when":"POST /admin/price-lists is called"}],"ears":"If a signed-in user calls an endpoint that their role does not permit, then the portal shall return status 403.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Buyer of Acme Garage and order ORD-000200 belonging to Fleet Co","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 404 and no order fields are returned","when":"GET /orders/ORD-000200 is called"},{"given":"A Buyer of Acme Garage and invoice INV-000050 belonging to Fleet Co","id":"AC-10.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 404 and no PDF file is returned","when":"GET /invoices/INV-000050/pdf is called"},{"given":"Acme Garage has 3 orders and Fleet Co has 2 orders","id":"AC-10.3","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains exactly the 3 Acme Garage orders","when":"A Buyer of Acme Garage calls GET /orders"}],"ears":"If a Buyer requests an order, invoice, price list, delivery address or company account record that belongs to another customer company, then the portal shall return status 404.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-5","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Administrator and an order in status Received","id":"AC-11.1","level":"api","then":"Both response statuses are 200 and the order record status value is 'Confirmed'","when":"GET /staff/orders is called and then POST /staff/orders/{id}/confirm is called"}],"ears":"The portal shall grant the Administrator role every Office Staff capability.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-6","ASM-28"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Administrator and active company Acme Garage","id":"AC-12.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201, the user record has status 'Invited' and one invitation email is sent to new@acme.test","when":"POST /admin/users is called with name, email new@acme.test, role Buyer and company Acme Garage"},{"given":"A signed-in Administrator","id":"AC-12.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 with error code INVALID_ROLE and no user row is created","when":"POST /admin/users is called with role 'Customer Account Manager'"}],"ears":"When an Administrator invites a user with role Buyer (linked to a customer company) or Office Staff, the portal shall create the user in status Invited and send an invitation email with a link valid for the configured invitation period (default 7 days).","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","Q-1","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An invitation sent 2 days ago to new@acme.test","id":"AC-13.1","level":"api","then":"The user record status is 'Active' and the sign-in response status is 200","when":"The user submits password 'Start#123' via the invitation link and then signs in"},{"given":"An invitation sent 7 days and 1 minute ago","id":"AC-13.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 with error code LINK_EXPIRED and the user record status remains 'Invited'","when":"The user submits a password via the invitation link"}],"ears":"When an invited user sets a password through an unexpired invitation link, the portal shall change the user's status to Active.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user in status Invited with an earlier invitation link L1","id":"AC-14.1","level":"api","then":"A new invitation email is sent and the L1 submission response status is 400 with error code LINK_USED","when":"POST /admin/users/{id}/resend-invitation is called and the user then submits a password via L1"}],"ears":"When an Administrator resends an invitation to a user in status Invited, the portal shall send a new invitation email and invalidate all earlier invitation links for that user.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Buyer who placed order ORD-000123 and is then deactivated","id":"AC-15.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 with error code ACCOUNT_INACTIVE","when":"The Buyer calls POST /auth/sign-in with the correct password"},{"given":"The deactivated Buyer still holds a session token issued before deactivation","id":"AC-15.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401 and no order row is created","when":"POST /orders is called with that token"},{"given":"The deactivated Buyer's order ORD-000123","id":"AC-15.3","level":"api","then":"ORD-000123 is in the returned list with its original placed-by value","when":"Another Buyer of the same company calls GET /orders"}],"ears":"When an Administrator deactivates a user, the portal shall block that user's sign-in and order submission while keeping every order and invoice record linked to that user.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","I-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A deactivated Buyer of active company Acme Garage","id":"AC-16.1","level":"api","then":"The user record status is 'Active' and the sign-in response status is 200","when":"POST /admin/users/{id}/reactivate is called and the Buyer signs in"},{"given":"A deactivated Buyer of inactive company Fleet Co","id":"AC-16.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code COMPANY_INACTIVE","when":"POST /admin/users/{id}/reactivate is called"}],"ears":"When an Administrator reactivates a deactivated user whose customer company is active, the portal shall allow that user to sign in again.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Users in statuses Invited, Active and Deactivated","id":"AC-17.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list shows each user's role, company and status field values","when":"An Administrator calls GET /admin/users"},{"given":"An Active Buyer of Acme Garage","id":"AC-17.2","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains only Fleet Co orders","when":"An Administrator changes the user's company to Fleet Co and the user then calls GET /orders"}],"ears":"The portal shall let Administrators list users with role, linked company and account status, change a user's role between Buyer and Office Staff, and change a Buyer's linked customer company.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-9","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active Buyer of company Fleet Co, which an Administrator has set inactive","id":"AC-18.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 with error code COMPANY_INACTIVE","when":"The Buyer calls POST /auth/sign-in with correct credentials"},{"given":"A Buyer of Fleet Co holding a session from before the company was set inactive","id":"AC-18.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401 or 403 and no order row is created","when":"POST /orders is called"}],"ears":"While a customer company is inactive, the portal shall reject sign-in and order submission by that company's users.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-5","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Inactive company Fleet Co","id":"AC-19.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code COMPANY_INACTIVE and no order row is created","when":"Office Staff call POST /staff/orders for Fleet Co with valid lines"}],"ears":"While a customer company is inactive, the portal shall reject staff-created orders for that company.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-8","I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Fleet Co is inactive and its order ORD-000300 is Out for delivery","id":"AC-20.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and an invoice row for ORD-000300 is created","when":"Office Staff set ORD-000300 to Delivered"},{"given":"Fleet Co is inactive","id":"AC-20.2","level":"api","then":"Both response statuses are 200 and the returned lists include Fleet Co's orders and invoices","when":"Office Staff call GET /staff/orders?customer=FleetCo and GET /staff/invoices?customer=FleetCo"}],"ears":"While a customer company is inactive, the portal shall continue to process that company's existing orders through status changes and invoice creation and keep them visible to staff.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-5","Q-8","I-14","I-16"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Administrator","id":"AC-21.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the company row holds every submitted field value","when":"POST /admin/companies is called with all listed fields and account number C-1001"},{"given":"A company with account number C-1001 exists","id":"AC-21.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code DUPLICATE_ACCOUNT_NUMBER","when":"POST /admin/companies is called with account number C-1001"}],"ears":"The portal shall let Administrators create and edit customer companies with company name, unique account number, primary contact, contact email, contact phone, billing address, assigned price list and active/inactive status.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Office Staff user and company Acme Garage","id":"AC-22.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and an address row linked to Acme Garage is created","when":"POST /staff/companies/{id}/addresses is called with all address fields"},{"given":"A signed-in Buyer of Acme Garage","id":"AC-22.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and no address row is created","when":"POST /companies/me/addresses is called"}],"ears":"The portal shall let only Office Staff and Administrators add, edit and remove a customer company's delivery addresses, each with label, address lines 1 and 2, city, state/region, postal code, country, contact person and contact phone.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-7","ASM-13","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Acme Garage has 2 delivery addresses and Fleet Co has 1","id":"AC-23.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains exactly the 2 Acme Garage addresses with all address fields","when":"A Buyer of Acme Garage calls GET /companies/me/addresses"}],"ears":"When a Buyer requests their company's delivery addresses, the portal shall return every delivery address of the Buyer's own company.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","Q-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Companies 'Acme Garage' (C-1001) and 'Fleet Co' (C-2001)","id":"AC-24.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains Acme Garage and not Fleet Co","when":"Office Staff call GET /staff/companies?q=acme"},{"given":"Company Acme Garage with users, addresses, orders and invoices","id":"AC-24.2","level":"api","then":"The response contains the company fields plus the users, addresses, price list, orders and invoices lists","when":"Office Staff call GET /staff/companies/{id}"}],"ears":"The portal shall let Office Staff list all customer companies, search them by company name or account number with partial matching, and view a company's details, users, addresses, assigned price list, orders and invoices.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active product 'Brake Pad Set' and retired product 'Old Filter'","id":"AC-25.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains 'Brake Pad Set' with all listed fields and does not contain 'Old Filter'","when":"A Buyer calls GET /catalogue/products"}],"ears":"When a Buyer browses the catalogue, the portal shall return only active products, each with image URL, name, distributor product code, manufacturer, unit of sale, pack size, the Buyer's price and stock status.","id":"REQ-25","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-2","I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active product 'Brake Pad Set' with manufacturer part number 'BP-1234' and brand 'Brembo'","id":"AC-26.1","level":"api","then":"Each returned list contains 'Brake Pad Set'","when":"GET /catalogue/products?q=brak, ?q=bp-12 and ?q=BREM are called"},{"given":"Retired product 'Brake Drum Old'","id":"AC-26.2","level":"api","then":"'Brake Drum Old' is not in the returned list","when":"GET /catalogue/products?q=brake is called"}],"ears":"When a Buyer searches the catalogue with a text term, the portal shall return active products whose name, distributor product code, manufacturer part number or brand contains the term, ignoring letter case.","id":"REQ-26","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"3 active products in 'Filters' and 5 in 'Brake system'","id":"AC-27.1","level":"api","then":"The first returned list has exactly the 3 Filters products and the second returned list has all 8 products","when":"GET /catalogue/products?category=filters is called, then GET /catalogue/products with no category"}],"ears":"When a Buyer selects a category filter, the portal shall return only active products assigned to that category, and when the filter is cleared it shall return all active products.","id":"REQ-27","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-2","ASM-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product A compatible with Ford Focus 2018 1.0 EcoBoost petrol, product B compatible with Ford Fiesta 2018","id":"AC-28.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains product A and not product B","when":"GET /catalogue/products?make=Ford&model=Focus&year=2018 is called"},{"given":"Product A compatible only with petrol Ford Focus 2018","id":"AC-28.2","level":"api","then":"The returned list is empty","when":"GET /catalogue/products?make=Ford&model=Focus&year=2018&fuel=diesel is called"}],"ears":"When a Buyer searches by vehicle using any combination of make, model, year, engine, fuel type and variant, the portal shall return only active products that have a compatibility entry matching every supplied value.","id":"REQ-28","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active product 'Brake Pad Set' with 2 vehicle compatibility entries","id":"AC-29.1","level":"api","then":"The response contains every listed field and the compatibility list has 2 entries","when":"A Buyer calls GET /catalogue/products/{id}"},{"given":"Product 'Brake Pad Set' with imported quantity 0","id":"AC-29.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the stock status value is 'Out of stock'","when":"A Buyer calls GET /catalogue/products/{id}"}],"ears":"When a Buyer opens an active product, the portal shall return its image URL, name, product code, manufacturer, description, unit, pack size, the Buyer's price, stock status and list of compatible vehicles.","id":"REQ-29","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P priced 50.00 on 'Standard' and 40.00 on 'Workshop A'; Acme Garage is assigned 'Workshop A'","id":"AC-30.1","level":"api","then":"The returned price value is 40.00 and the value 50.00 does not appear in the response","when":"A Buyer of Acme Garage calls GET /catalogue/products/{P}"}],"ears":"When a Buyer views a product, the portal shall show the unit price from the price list assigned to the Buyer's company.","id":"REQ-30","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product Q has no price on Acme Garage's assigned list","id":"AC-31.1","level":"api","then":"The returned price field is null and the price label value is 'Price on request'","when":"A Buyer of Acme Garage calls GET /catalogue/products/{Q}"},{"given":"The same product Q","id":"AC-31.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 with error code NO_PRICE and the basket line count is unchanged","when":"The Buyer calls POST /basket/lines for Q with quantity 1"}],"ears":"If a product has no price on the Buyer's company price list, then the portal shall show 'Price on request' for that product and reject adding it to the basket.","id":"REQ-31","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-3","I-3","I-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Administrator","id":"AC-32.1","level":"api","then":"Both response statuses are 2xx and the price list row 'Fleet' has one price row for P with value 42.50","when":"POST /admin/price-lists creates 'Fleet', then PUT sets product P to 42.50"},{"given":"Price list 'Fleet' already has a price for product P","id":"AC-32.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code DUPLICATE_PRICE","when":"POST /admin/price-lists/{Fleet}/prices is called again for P"}],"ears":"The portal shall let Administrators create, rename and deactivate price lists and add, edit and remove product prices on a price list, with at most one price per product per list.","id":"REQ-32","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Acme Garage on 'Standard' (P = 50.00) and 'Workshop A' has P = 40.00","id":"AC-33.1","level":"api","then":"The returned price value is 40.00","when":"An Administrator assigns 'Workshop A' to Acme Garage and a Buyer of Acme Garage calls GET /catalogue/products/{P}"}],"ears":"When an Administrator assigns or changes a customer company's price list, the portal shall use the new list's prices for that company's catalogue, basket, staff-created orders and repeat orders from then on.","id":"REQ-33","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Order ORD-000123 has a line for P at unit price 40.00","id":"AC-34.1","level":"api","then":"The returned line unit price value is 40.00","when":"An Administrator changes P on the customer's list to 45.00 and GET /orders/ORD-000123 is called"}],"ears":"When a price on a price list changes, the portal shall keep the unit prices stored on existing orders and invoices unchanged.","id":"REQ-34","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Acme Garage is assigned 'Workshop A' with P = 40.00","id":"AC-35.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned price value is 40.00","when":"Office Staff call GET /staff/products/{P}/price?company=AcmeGarage"}],"ears":"The portal shall let Office Staff view the unit price any customer company pays for a product.","id":"REQ-35","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The low-stock threshold setting is 5","id":"AC-36.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned values are 'Out of stock', 'Low stock', 'Low stock' and 'In stock'","when":"StockStatusCalculator.statusFor is called with quantities 0, 1, 5 and 6"}],"ears":"The stock status calculator shall return 'Out of stock' for a quantity of 0 or less, 'Low stock' for a quantity from 1 up to the configured low-stock threshold, and 'In stock' for a quantity above that threshold.","id":"REQ-36","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","I-3","ASM-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P has quantity 2 and a valid CSV in the configured folder lists P with quantity 30","id":"AC-37.1","level":"job","then":"Product P's stock row has quantity 30 and status 'In stock', and an import log record has status 'Success' with the count of rows applied","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"When the scheduled stock import runs and finds a valid ERP CSV file in the configured location, the portal shall update the stock quantity and stock status of every product named in a row with a known product identifier.","id":"REQ-37","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A valid CSV with rows for known product P (quantity 7) and unknown identifier 'ZZ-999'","id":"AC-38.1","level":"job","then":"Product P's stock quantity value is 7 and the import log record lists 'ZZ-999' under skipped identifiers","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"If an ERP CSV row has a product identifier unknown to the portal, then the stock import shall skip that row, apply the other valid rows and list the unknown identifier in the import log.","id":"REQ-38","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-6","I-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P has quantity 12 and the CSV has quantity 'abc' on one row","id":"AC-39.1","level":"job","then":"Product P's stock quantity value is still 12 and an import log record has status 'Failed' with a reason naming the bad row","when":"The stock import job runs"},{"given":"No CSV file is present at the configured location","id":"AC-39.2","level":"job","then":"An import log record has status 'Failed' with reason 'file missing' and no stock row changes","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"If the ERP CSV file is missing, unreadable, lacks a required column or contains a non-numeric or negative quantity, then the stock import shall keep all previous stock data and record a failed import log entry with the reason.","id":"REQ-39","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The latest import log record has status 'Failed'","id":"AC-40.1","level":"api","then":"The dashboard response field latestImportFailed is true and the import list shows the failed record with time and reason","when":"Office Staff call GET /staff/dashboard and GET /staff/stock-imports"}],"ears":"When the most recent stock import has failed, the portal shall show the failure time and reason to Office Staff and Administrators in the import log list and on the staff dashboard.","id":"REQ-40","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Outbound traffic to the ERP host is recorded and the ERP CSV file checksum is noted","id":"AC-41.1","level":"job","then":"No outbound call to the ERP host is recorded and the CSV file checksum value is unchanged","when":"The stock import job runs and a Buyer submits an order"}],"ears":"The portal shall not send any create, update or delete request to the ERP system.","id":"REQ-41","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P imported with quantity 30 at 02:00","id":"AC-42.1","level":"api","then":"The response contains quantity 30, status 'In stock' and last import time 02:00","when":"Office Staff call GET /staff/products/{P}/stock"}],"ears":"The portal shall let Office Staff view each product's imported quantity, stock status and the time of the last successful import.","id":"REQ-42","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P has imported quantity 10 and a price on the Buyer's list","id":"AC-43.1","level":"api","then":"The first response status is 200; the second response status is 400 with error code QUANTITY_EXCEEDS_STOCK and the line quantity value stays 10","when":"POST /basket/lines is called for P with quantity 10, then PUT changes it to 11"},{"given":"Product R has imported quantity 0","id":"AC-43.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 with error code OUT_OF_STOCK","when":"POST /basket/lines is called for R with quantity 1"}],"ears":"When a Buyer adds a product to the basket or changes a basket line quantity, the portal shall accept the line only if the product is active, priced for the Buyer's company and the quantity is from 1 to the product's imported stock quantity.","id":"REQ-43","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-4","I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A basket with 2 x P at 12.50 and 1 x Q at 10.00","id":"AC-44.1","level":"api","then":"The returned line totals are 25.00 and 10.00 and the subtotal value is 35.00","when":"GET /basket is called"},{"given":"The same basket","id":"AC-44.2","level":"api","then":"The returned list has one line and the subtotal value is 25.00","when":"DELETE /basket/lines/{Q} is called and then GET /basket"}],"ears":"The portal shall return each basket line with unit price, quantity and line total, and the basket subtotal, all excluding tax.","id":"REQ-44","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Buyer with 2 basket lines","id":"AC-45.1","level":"api","then":"The returned basket has the same 2 lines","when":"The Buyer calls GET /catalogue/products and then GET /basket in the same session"},{"given":"The same Buyer","id":"AC-45.2","level":"api","then":"The returned basket line count is 0","when":"The Buyer signs out, signs in again and calls GET /basket"}],"ears":"While a Buyer's session is active, the portal shall keep the basket contents across page navigation and discard them when the session ends.","id":"REQ-45","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Cutoff 14:00, Saturdays and Sundays configured as non-working","id":"AC-46.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned values are Tuesday, Wednesday and Wednesday","when":"DeliveryDateCalculator.earliestDate is called for Monday 13:00, Monday 14:00 and Monday 15:00"},{"given":"The same settings","id":"AC-46.2","level":"unit","then":"The returned values are the following Monday and the following Tuesday","when":"DeliveryDateCalculator.earliestDate is called for Friday 13:00 and Friday 15:00"},{"given":"The same settings plus Tuesday configured as a non-working holiday","id":"AC-46.3","level":"unit","then":"The returned value is Wednesday","when":"DeliveryDateCalculator.earliestDate is called for Monday 13:00"}],"ears":"The delivery date calculator shall return as earliest delivery date the next working day for an order time before the configured cutoff (default 14:00) and the working day after the next working day for an order time at or after the cutoff, using the configured timezone and non-working dates.","id":"REQ-46","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-11","ASM-36"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Now is Monday 15:00, earliest date is Wednesday, maximum days ahead is 30","id":"AC-47.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 with error code INVALID_DELIVERY_DATE and no order row is created","when":"POST /orders is submitted with delivery date Tuesday"},{"given":"The same settings","id":"AC-47.2","level":"api","then":"Each response status is 400 with error code INVALID_DELIVERY_DATE","when":"POST /orders is submitted with a Saturday date, or a date 31 days ahead"}],"ears":"If a delivery date submitted by a Buyer or staff is not a working day between the earliest delivery date and the configured maximum number of days ahead, then the portal shall reject it.","id":"REQ-47","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Buyer of Acme Garage and an address belonging to Fleet Co","id":"AC-48.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 with error code INVALID_ADDRESS and no order row is created","when":"POST /orders is submitted with the Fleet Co address id"}],"ears":"If a submitted delivery address does not belong to the order's customer company, then the portal shall reject the order or edit.","id":"REQ-48","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","Q-4","Q-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A basket with 2 lines, a chosen address, date and note 'Rear entrance'","id":"AC-49.1","level":"api","then":"The response contains both lines with prices and totals, the subtotal, the address, the date and the note value 'Rear entrance'","when":"GET /checkout/review is called"}],"ears":"When a Buyer requests the checkout review, the portal shall return the basket lines, unit prices, line totals, subtotal, selected delivery address, selected delivery date and order note.","id":"REQ-49","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A basket line for P added at 40.00 and P's list price changed to 42.00 before submission","id":"AC-50.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code CHECKOUT_CHANGED, the returned list names P with price 42.00, and no order row is created","when":"POST /orders is called"},{"given":"A basket line for 8 x R and R's imported quantity dropped to 5 before submission","id":"AC-50.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 and the returned list names R with available quantity 5","when":"POST /orders is called"}],"ears":"When a Buyer submits an order, the portal shall re-check every line's stock limit and current price and, if any line fails, reject the submission with a list of the failing lines and their current price or available quantity.","id":"REQ-50","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The last order number is ORD-000123 and a valid basket","id":"AC-51.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 with order number ORD-000124 and the order row has status 'Received', the lines with their unit prices, address, date and note","when":"A Buyer calls POST /orders"},{"given":"The order ORD-000124 just created","id":"AC-51.2","level":"api","then":"ORD-000124 is in the returned list","when":"Office Staff call GET /staff/orders?status=Received"}],"ears":"When a valid order is submitted, the portal shall create an order with the next sequential order number, the lines at order-time unit prices, the delivery address, the delivery date, the optional note and status Received.","id":"REQ-51","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-13","ASM-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Order ORD-000124 placed by Buyer B and confirmed by staff user S","id":"AC-52.1","level":"api","then":"The returned timeline list has entries 'Received' by B and 'Confirmed' by S, each with a timestamp","when":"GET /orders/ORD-000124 is called"}],"ears":"When an order changes status, the portal shall add a timeline entry recording the new status, the date and time, and the user or 'system' that made the change.","id":"REQ-52","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-8","I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Orders for Acme Garage (Received, Confirmed) and Fleet Co (Received)","id":"AC-53.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains only the Acme Garage Received order with all listed fields","when":"Office Staff call GET /staff/orders?customer=AcmeGarage&status=Received"},{"given":"Orders placed on 1 and 3 October","id":"AC-53.2","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains only the 3 October order","when":"Office Staff call GET /staff/orders?from=2026-10-02&to=2026-10-03"}],"ears":"The portal shall show Office Staff an order queue of all orders with order number, customer, order date, requested delivery date, order total and current status, filterable by customer, order date range and status.","id":"REQ-53","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-14","I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order with delivery date Thursday and now is Tuesday 15:00 (earliest date Thursday)","id":"AC-54.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 with error code INVALID_DELIVERY_DATE and the order delivery date value stays Thursday","when":"Office Staff PATCH the delivery date to Wednesday"},{"given":"A Received order with 2 lines","id":"AC-54.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, the order record has 1 line, the new note, and a recalculated total","when":"Office Staff PATCH to remove one line and change the note"}],"ears":"While an order is in status Received, the portal shall let Office Staff change line quantities, remove lines, change the order note, change the delivery address to another address of the same company and change the delivery date to a date valid under the cutoff rule calculated at the time of the edit.","id":"REQ-54","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","Q-4","ASM-35"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order placed by Buyer B with 10 x P","id":"AC-55.1","level":"api","then":"An amendment record with old 10, new 6, staff user and time is returned in the order detail, and one email listing P 10 -> 6 is sent to B","when":"Office Staff change P to 6"},{"given":"A Received order","id":"AC-55.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and no email is sent","when":"Office Staff change only the delivery address"}],"ears":"When Office Staff change a line quantity or remove a line on a Received order, the portal shall record the amendment with old quantity, new quantity, user and time, and send the customer an email describing the change.","id":"REQ-55","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-33","ASM-35","I-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An order in status Confirmed","id":"AC-56.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code ORDER_NOT_EDITABLE and the line quantity value is unchanged","when":"Office Staff PATCH a line quantity"}],"ears":"If Office Staff attempt to edit lines, note, delivery address or delivery date of an order that is not in status Received, then the portal shall reject the edit.","id":"REQ-56","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order ORD-000124 placed by Buyer B, all lines in stock","id":"AC-57.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, the order record status is 'Confirmed' with confirmedBy S and a timestamp, and one email is sent to B","when":"Staff user S calls POST /staff/orders/ORD-000124/confirm"},{"given":"A Received order with a line for 8 x R and R's imported quantity is 5","id":"AC-57.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code STOCK_INSUFFICIENT naming R and the order status value stays 'Received'","when":"Staff call POST /staff/orders/{id}/confirm"}],"ears":"When Office Staff confirm a Received order whose lines are all within imported stock and whose delivery address still exists, the portal shall set the status to Confirmed, record the confirming user and time, and send the confirmation email.","id":"REQ-57","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-33"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Order ORD-000124 where staff changed P from 10 to 6 before confirming","id":"AC-58.1","level":"api","then":"The sent email contains 'ORD-000124', every line, the total, address, date and the text showing P 10 -> 6","when":"The order is confirmed"}],"ears":"When a confirmation email is sent, the portal shall include the order number, lines with quantities and unit prices, order total, delivery address, delivery date and every quantity change staff made before confirmation.","id":"REQ-58","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An order in status Confirmed","id":"AC-59.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the order status value is 'Picking'","when":"Office Staff set the status to Picking"},{"given":"An order in status Confirmed","id":"AC-59.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code INVALID_TRANSITION and the status value stays 'Confirmed'","when":"Office Staff set the status to Out for delivery"},{"given":"An order in status Picking","id":"AC-59.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code INVALID_TRANSITION","when":"Office Staff set the status to Confirmed"}],"ears":"When Office Staff change the status of a confirmed order, the portal shall allow only the next step in the sequence Confirmed, Picking, Out for delivery, Delivered.","id":"REQ-59","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Order ORD-000124 placed by Buyer B in status Picking","id":"AC-60.1","level":"api","then":"One email is sent to B containing 'ORD-000124' and the text 'out for delivery'","when":"Office Staff set the status to Out for delivery"}],"ears":"When an order's status changes to Out for delivery, the portal shall send an email that names the order number and states that the order is out for delivery.","id":"REQ-60","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-5","ASM-33"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An order placed by Buyer B in status Picking","id":"AC-61.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, the order record has status 'Cancelled' with the reason, user and time, and one email with the reason is sent to B","when":"Staff call POST /staff/orders/{id}/cancel with reason 'Customer request by phone'"},{"given":"A Received order","id":"AC-61.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 with error code REASON_REQUIRED and the status value stays 'Received'","when":"Staff call POST /staff/orders/{id}/cancel with an empty reason"},{"given":"A Delivered order","id":"AC-61.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code INVALID_TRANSITION","when":"Staff call POST /staff/orders/{id}/cancel with a reason"}],"ears":"When Office Staff reject or cancel an order that is not Delivered or Cancelled, the portal shall require a reason, set the status to Cancelled, record the reason, user and time, and send the customer a cancellation email.","id":"REQ-61","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","Q-3","ASM-16","ASM-34"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A staff-created order for Acme Garage whose contact email is orders@acme.test","id":"AC-62.1","level":"api","then":"The confirmation email is sent to orders@acme.test and not to any Buyer","when":"The order is confirmed"}],"ears":"The portal shall send order emails to the Buyer who placed the order, or to the company contact email when the order was created by staff.","id":"REQ-62","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-33","ASM-17","I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active company Acme Garage on 'Workshop A' with P = 40.00","id":"AC-63.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the order row has status 'Received', unit price 40.00, createdByStaff true and createdBy S","when":"Staff user S calls POST /staff/orders for Acme Garage with 3 x P, a company address and a valid date"},{"given":"The staff-created order above","id":"AC-63.2","level":"api","then":"The order is in the returned list","when":"A Buyer of Acme Garage calls GET /orders"}],"ears":"When Office Staff submit an order for an active customer company with a company delivery address, products, quantities, a valid delivery date and optional notes, the portal shall create the order at that company's price-list prices in status Received and mark it as created by staff.","id":"REQ-63","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","I-14","ASM-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"For 2026-10-07 there are orders A (Confirmed), B (Out for delivery) and C (Cancelled), plus order D for 2026-10-08","id":"AC-64.1","level":"api","then":"The returned file has a header row and exactly 2 data rows, for A and B, with all listed columns","when":"Office Staff call GET /staff/delivery-list.csv?date=2026-10-07"}],"ears":"When Office Staff export the delivery list for a date (default today), the portal shall return a CSV file of all orders with that requested delivery date that are not Cancelled, with order number, customer, delivery address, contact name and phone, delivery date, order lines, note and status.","id":"REQ-64","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","ASM-27"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"2 Received, 1 Confirmed, 3 Picking, 1 Out for delivery orders, 2 orders due today, 4 Unpaid and 1 Overdue invoices","id":"AC-65.1","level":"api","then":"The response count fields hold 2, 1, 3, 1, 2, 4 and 1 and the latest import status field is present","when":"Office Staff call GET /staff/dashboard"}],"ears":"The portal shall show Office Staff a dashboard with counts of Received orders, Confirmed orders, Picking orders, Out for delivery orders, orders due for delivery today, Unpaid and Overdue invoices, and the latest stock import result.","id":"REQ-65","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Acme Garage has orders placed by Buyer B1, Buyer B2 and staff","id":"AC-66.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains all 3 orders with the listed fields","when":"Buyer B1 calls GET /orders"},{"given":"Acme Garage has one Delivered and one Received order","id":"AC-66.2","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains only the Delivered order","when":"Buyer B1 calls GET /orders?status=Delivered"}],"ears":"When a Buyer views order history, the portal shall return every order of the Buyer's company, including staff-created orders, with order number, order date, delivery date, delivery address, total and status, filterable by order date range and status.","id":"REQ-66","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-15","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Acme Garage order with 2 lines and 1 staff quantity amendment","id":"AC-67.1","level":"api","then":"The response contains every listed field, 2 line records and 1 amendment record","when":"A Buyer of Acme Garage calls GET /orders/{id}"}],"ears":"When a Buyer opens one of their company's orders, the portal shall return order number, order date, customer, delivery address, requested delivery date, current status, status timeline, lines with quantities, unit prices and line totals, order total, order note and staff amendments.","id":"REQ-67","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order of Acme Garage placed by staff","id":"AC-68.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, the order status value is 'Cancelled' and the timeline has a 'Cancelled' entry by B1","when":"Buyer B1 of Acme Garage calls POST /orders/{id}/cancel"}],"ears":"When a Buyer cancels a company order that is in status Received, the portal shall set the status to Cancelled and record the Buyer and time in the timeline.","id":"REQ-68","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Acme Garage order in status Confirmed","id":"AC-69.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code NOT_CANCELLABLE, the message tells the Buyer to contact the office, and the status value stays 'Confirmed'","when":"A Buyer of Acme Garage calls POST /orders/{id}/cancel"}],"ears":"If a Buyer attempts to cancel an order that is not in status Received, then the portal shall reject the cancellation and tell the Buyer to contact the distributor office.","id":"REQ-69","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Order ORD-000100 had 5 x P at 38.00, 2 x R (now retired) and 4 x S (now out of stock); P now costs 40.00","id":"AC-70.1","level":"api","then":"The returned basket has one line 5 x P at 40.00, the returned unavailable list names R and S, and the company's order count is unchanged","when":"A Buyer of the same company calls POST /orders/ORD-000100/repeat"}],"ears":"When a Buyer repeats a company order, the portal shall add each line whose product is active, priced and in stock to the basket at the current price-list price, capped at the imported stock quantity, flag every other line as unavailable, and create no order.","id":"REQ-70","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15","Q-6","ASM-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Order ORD-000124 with net total 100.00 is Out for delivery, tax rate is 20% and the last invoice is INV-000049","id":"AC-71.1","level":"api","then":"An invoice row INV-000050 is created for ORD-000124 with net 100.00, tax 20.00, gross 120.00 and status 'Unpaid'","when":"Office Staff set the status to Delivered"},{"given":"An order in status Picking","id":"AC-71.2","level":"api","then":"No invoice for that order is in the returned list","when":"GET /invoices is called by a Buyer of that company"}],"ears":"When an order's status becomes Delivered, the portal shall create an invoice with the next sequential invoice number, customer, billing address, order number, invoice date, lines with quantities and unit prices, net total, configured tax rate, tax amount, gross total and payment status Unpaid.","id":"REQ-71","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","ASM-2","ASM-9","ASM-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Overdue days setting is 30 and today is 2026-10-31","id":"AC-72.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned values are 'Unpaid', 'Overdue' and 'Paid'","when":"InvoiceStatusCalculator.statusFor is called for unpaid invoices dated 2026-10-01 and 2026-09-30 and a paid invoice dated 2026-09-01"}],"ears":"The invoice status calculator shall return 'Overdue' for an unpaid invoice whose invoice date is more than the configured number of overdue days before today, 'Unpaid' for any other unpaid invoice, and 'Paid' for a paid invoice.","id":"REQ-72","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","ASM-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Acme Garage has invoices for orders placed by B1 and by B2","id":"AC-73.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains both invoices with the listed fields","when":"Buyer B1 calls GET /invoices"}],"ears":"When a Buyer views invoices, the portal shall return every invoice of the Buyer's company with invoice number, order number, invoice date, gross total and payment status.","id":"REQ-73","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-16","Q-2","ASM-32"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Invoice INV-000050 of Acme Garage","id":"AC-74.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 with content type application/pdf and the file text contains 'INV-000050', 'ORD-000124', the billing address and the gross total 120.00","when":"A Buyer of Acme Garage calls GET /invoices/INV-000050/pdf"}],"ears":"When a Buyer or Office Staff user downloads an invoice they may access, the portal shall return a PDF file containing the client's logo and company details, invoice number, customer, billing address, order number, invoice date, lines, quantities, unit prices, net, tax and gross totals and payment status.","id":"REQ-74","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","ASM-26"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Unpaid invoices for Acme Garage and Fleet Co and a paid invoice for Acme Garage","id":"AC-75.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains only the unpaid Acme Garage invoice","when":"Office Staff call GET /staff/invoices?customer=AcmeGarage&status=Unpaid"}],"ears":"The portal shall let Office Staff list and view all invoices, filterable by customer and payment status.","id":"REQ-75","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Unpaid invoice INV-000050","id":"AC-76.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the invoice record has status 'Paid', payment date 2026-10-20 and recordedBy S","when":"Staff user S calls POST /staff/invoices/INV-000050/payment with date 2026-10-20"},{"given":"Invoice INV-000050 already Paid","id":"AC-76.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code ALREADY_PAID","when":"Staff call POST /staff/invoices/INV-000050/payment again"},{"given":"Unpaid invoice INV-000051 and today is 2026-10-20","id":"AC-76.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 with error code INVALID_PAYMENT_DATE","when":"Staff call POST /staff/invoices/INV-000051/payment with date 2026-10-21"}],"ears":"When Office Staff mark an unpaid invoice as paid with a payment date no later than today, the portal shall set the payment status to Paid and record the payment date and the recording user.","id":"REQ-76","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Administrator","id":"AC-77.1","level":"api","then":"The first response status is 201 and the second response status is 409 with error code DUPLICATE_PRODUCT_CODE","when":"POST /admin/products is called with all fields and code 'BP-1234', then again with code 'BP-1234'"},{"given":"Product P on delivered order ORD-000100","id":"AC-77.2","level":"api","then":"The order detail still returns the line for P and P is not in the catalogue list","when":"An Administrator retires P and a Buyer calls GET /orders/ORD-000100 and GET /catalogue/products"}],"ears":"The portal shall let Administrators add, edit and retire products with name, manufacturer part number, unique distributor product code, description, category, manufacturer/brand, unit of sale and pack size, keeping retired products on historical orders and invoices.","id":"REQ-77","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Administrator","id":"AC-78.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 with error code NESTED_CATEGORY_NOT_SUPPORTED","when":"POST /admin/categories is called with name 'Filters' and a parent category id"},{"given":"Category 'Exhaust' retired by an Administrator","id":"AC-78.2","level":"api","then":"'Exhaust' is not in the returned list","when":"A Buyer calls GET /catalogue/categories"}],"ears":"The portal shall let Administrators create, edit and retire single-level categories and assign each product to one category, hiding retired categories from the catalogue filter.","id":"REQ-78","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-10","ASM-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A 2 MB PNG file","id":"AC-79.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the product's image URL field points to the stored file","when":"An Administrator calls POST /admin/products/{id}/image"},{"given":"A 12 MB JPEG file and a 1 MB GIF file","id":"AC-79.2","level":"api","then":"Each response status is 400 with error codes FILE_TOO_LARGE and UNSUPPORTED_TYPE and the image URL value is unchanged","when":"An Administrator uploads each"}],"ears":"When an Administrator uploads or replaces a product image, the portal shall accept only JPEG, PNG or WebP files of at most 10 MB and store them in cloud storage.","id":"REQ-79","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-29"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P with no compatibility entries","id":"AC-80.1","level":"api","then":"GET /catalogue/products/{P} returns a compatibility list with 2 entries","when":"An Administrator adds entries for Ford Focus 2018 and VW Golf 2019"}],"ears":"The portal shall let Administrators add and remove vehicle compatibility entries (make, model, model year, engine, fuel type, variant) on a product, with any number of entries per product.","id":"REQ-80","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-10","ASM-23"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Cutoff time setting is 14:00","id":"AC-81.1","level":"api","then":"The settings response status is 200 and the returned date value is Wednesday","when":"An Administrator sets it to 12:00 and DeliveryDateCalculator.earliestDate is called for Monday 13:00"},{"given":"A signed-in Office Staff user","id":"AC-81.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and the settings record is unchanged","when":"PUT /admin/settings is called"}],"ears":"The portal shall let Administrators change system settings for order cutoff time, timezone, non-working dates, maximum delivery days ahead, low-stock threshold, overdue days, tax rate, reset-link and invitation validity periods, order and invoice number prefixes, and invoice company details and logo.","id":"REQ-81","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-5","ASM-8","ASM-11","ASM-12","ASM-19","ASM-25","ASM-36"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P created by Administrator A1 and later edited by Administrator A2","id":"AC-82.1","level":"api","then":"The response fields show createdBy A1, createdAt, updatedBy A2 and updatedAt","when":"An Administrator calls GET /admin/products/{P}"}],"ears":"The portal shall store on every order, invoice, customer company, user, product, category and price list record who created it and when, and who last changed it and when, and show these values to Administrators.","id":"REQ-82","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","ASM-21"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"In October Acme Garage has 2 non-cancelled orders totalling 300.00 net and 1 cancelled order of 50.00","id":"AC-83.1","level":"api","then":"The returned customer row for Acme Garage shows count 2 and net total 300.00","when":"Office Staff call GET /staff/reports/sales?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31"},{"given":"The same data","id":"AC-83.2","level":"api","then":"The returned file contains the same customer and product rows as the on-screen response","when":"Office Staff call GET /staff/reports/sales.csv for the same range"}],"ears":"The portal shall provide Office Staff and Administrators a sales report for a chosen date range, filterable by customer, listing order count and net sales total per customer and quantity sold and net sales total per product from non-cancelled orders, with CSV export.","id":"REQ-83","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","ASM-20"]}],"suggestions":["Send emails when a customer cancels an order and when an invoice is created. ASM-18 left this unclear, so it is not specified here.","Reserve stock for Received and Confirmed orders, so two customers cannot order the same last units between imports.","Stop a price list from being deactivated while it is still assigned to a customer company, or warn the admin first.","Add two-factor sign-in for Office Staff and Administrator accounts.","Keep a full change history (old value and new value) for prices and customer accounts in a later release.","Add a CSV upload for vehicle compatibility data (ASM-23).","Add WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility as a goal for the Buyer screens.","Decide whether saved basket templates are shared within a company before they are built in a later release."]}],"models":["claude-opus-5-5","claude-opus-5-5","claude-opus-5-5"],"notes":["No OpenAI key: specify-other ran on claude-opus-5-5 (same family as the implementer)"]}